{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas","id":805117,"title":"Legacies 2ED Update ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-10T03:29:58-08:00","id":805117,"title":"Legacies 2ED Update ideas","content":"We are (hopefully) days before coming out of <b>Mage</b> 2ED corebook. I do not know about you, but I for <i>months</i> now want to make some clean up in 1ED Legacies rules, especially on Attainments Arcana. We now we will get few Legacies quickly updated by <b>DaveB </b>and team, but they cannot do all of them. <b>I hope that fan rules updates (and <i>only</i> rules updates ) - until the talked Legacies 2ED version is published on Onyx Path blog or in official books - are allowed?</b><br /> <br /> If yes, we need some uniformed topic markings for fan updates. I was thinking about <b>&quot;[Fan 2ED] ???&quot;</b> where ??? is group name. Maybe you have other idea on this?<br /> <br /> Beside resolving naming convention, I mark this topic as to place to talk how to stick to <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/legacies/\" target=\"_blank\">2ED Legacies paradigm with existing groups and how would you enforce it</a> ( without getting in to proper Attainments mechanics as we do not know how will spells exactly look like in 2ED, yet. ) Like those:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legacies Blog Post</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Path, Order or Praxis:</b> All Legacies possess an originating Path, and many (though not all) are connected to an Order\u2014Pentacle, Seer or Nameless.<br /> (\u2026)<br /> However, it is possible for a mage of any Path or Order to join a Legacy if she learns a Praxis that duplicates the Legacy\u2019s first Attainment, and utilizes one of the Legacy\u2019s Yantras.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcane (and Other) Knowledge:</b> Before initiation, your mage must possess at least two dots in the Legacy\u2019s new Ruling Arcanum. She must also possess two dots of Gnosis unless she\u2019s founding her own Legacy, which increases the requirement to three dots.<br /> Legacies also require other forms of knowledge based on their respective theories and beliefs. This normally takes the form of two or more dots in a particular Skill, but Storytellers and Legacy founders may specify additional requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have few groups on the target myself, mostly for mine own games to use. Here they are\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Acended Adepts</b> \u2013 <i>Obrimos and Adamanatine</i> Arrow \u2013 Their Attianments would focused on exploring and pefecting Astral Space by Mind as Ruling Arcanum and using Prime as Optional to unvealing the secret Truths and power connecting to the Astral Space in themselves and world around them. <b>Knowledge needed</b>: Meditative Mind 1 Merit, Occult 1<br /> <br /> <b>Blank Badges</b> \u2013 <i>Acanthus and Free Council </i>\u2013 Legacy with Mind as Ruling Arcanum for covering their identity and Fate as Optional to support their roles. They <i>are</i> The Invisibles of <b>Mage</b> universe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <b>Knowledge needed: </b>Occultation 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Forge Masters</b> \u2013 <i>Moros and Adamantine Arrow</i> \u2013 I hope we will get them in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> with Alchemy and Perfected Metals chapter, but if not, some neet tricks with Transmutations will be okay. Write up in 1ED marked them as having very large portion coming from Arrows, and this Legacy could nicely shown that Adamant Way is not all about war itself and not only Free Council has it\u2019s part of \u201ccraftsmen\u201d. <b>Knowledge needed: </b>Crafts 2<br /> <br /> <b>Logophages</b> \u2013 <i>Acanthus and Guardians of Veil</i> \u2013 Secret Keepers were previously marked as \u201cPath: Any\u201d but with changes to Legacies that <b>anyone</b> can learn it if he has proper Praxis \u2013 I think that sticking to one Path is crucial her. Logophages in 1ED had Mind as Primary and Fate as Secondary Arcanum, so they are tilled to the Path of Thorns. It also works with the premise of Legacy, as how like Acanthus maybe sure Secrets, once buried, <b>do not</b> \u2013 by accident \u2013 be uncovered once again. Also, Guardians need some Left-Hand Acanthus Legacy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <b>Knowledge needed: </b>Investigation 1, Occult 1 ( and sacrifice of ones memories )<br /> <br /> <b>Scions of God</b> \u2013 <i>Thyrsus and Silver Ladder</i> - Their Attainments would be focused on making Holy Guardian Angel as spirit being, with final transformation into one using Spirit as Ruling and Space as Optional. <b>Knowledge needed</b>: Persona Merit?, Occult 1<br /> <br /> <b>Tamers of Elements</b> \u2013 <i>Original Path and Nameless</i> \u2013 Their Attainments would largely be the same ( only <i>Tamers of Fire</i> should have switched places, with Mind as Ruling and Forces as Optional ), but Tamers in 1ED are described as Nameless Order onto itself, so the they should simply<b> be one</b>. It also have implication that Tamers are very popular in nuFree Council as alliance of Nameless. <b>Knowledge needed</b>: Occult 2 ( maybe other skills on case by case example )<br /> <br /> <b>The Quiescent </b>\u2013 <i>Moros and Guardians of Veil</i> \u2013 once again \u201cPath: Any\u201d group that should be just Guardians offshoot \u2013 well, maybe small Nameless Order on themselves. Ruling Arcana of Time and Optitonal as Death works for them. <b>Knowledge needed:</b> Science 1, Larceny 1 ( they want to pass magic as subtle tricks and new technology )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-10-2016, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T10:05:55-08:00","id":805318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>I hope that fan rules updates (and <i>only</i> rules updates ) - until the talked Legacies 2ED version is published on Onyx Path blog or in official books - are allowed?</b> </div> </div> </div>Huh ? Why shouldn't it be ? In RPGs you're expected to add or change rules as you want. People make &quot;my version off&quot; all the time, the only important part is that you don't take profit from it.<br /> <br /> I thought about making a Legacies update topic but lets wait until after the book is published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:57:46-08:00","id":805560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas#post805117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Forge Masters</b> \u2013 <i>Moros and Adamantine Arrow</i> \u2013 I hope we will get them in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> with Alchemy and Perfected Metals chapter, but if not, some neet tricks with Transmutations will be okay. Write up in 1ED marked them as having very large portion coming from Arrows, and this Legacy could nicely shown that Adamant Way is not all about war itself and not only Free Council has it\u2019s part of \u201ccraftsmen\u201d. <b>Knowledge needed: </b>Crafts 2</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Forge Masters are my all-time favorite legacy. I'd love to see them back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3812-thereby_become_a_monster","name":"Thereby_become_a_monster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T23:01:19-08:00","id":805827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas#post805117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Acended Adepts</b> \u2013 <i>Obrimos and Adamanatine</i> Arrow \u2013 Their Attianments would focused on exploring and pefecting Astral Space by Mind as Ruling Arcanum and using Prime as Optional to unvealing the secret Truths and power connecting to the Astral Space in themselves and world around them. <b>Knowledge needed</b>: Meditative Mind 1 Merit, Occult 1<br /> <br /> <b>Forge Masters</b> \u2013 <i>Moros and Adamantine Arrow</i> \u2013 I hope we will get them in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> with Alchemy and Perfected Metals chapter, but if not, some neet tricks with Transmutations will be okay. Write up in 1ED marked them as having very large portion coming from Arrows, and this Legacy could nicely shown that Adamant Way is not all about war itself and not only Free Council has it\u2019s part of \u201ccraftsmen\u201d. <b>Knowledge needed: </b>Crafts 2<br /> <br /> <b>Tamers of Elements</b> \u2013 <i>Original Path and Nameless</i> \u2013 Their Attainments would largely be the same ( only <i>Tamers of Fire</i> should have switched places, with Mind as Ruling and Forces as Optional ), but Tamers in 1ED are described as Nameless Order onto itself, so the they should simply<b> be one</b>. It also have implication that Tamers are very popular in nuFree Council as alliance of Nameless. <b>Knowledge needed</b>: Occult 2 ( maybe other skills on case by case example )</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely hoping for a write-up on these guys. And I'm definitely interested in seeing the Tamers as an alliance of Legacies that form their own Nameless Order. We definitely need some examples of Mages who <i>aren't</i> part of the Pentacle or Seers, <i>aren't</i> Scelesti or Reapers, <i>and</i> <i>aren't</i> Tremere, but at the same time are followers of an independent tradition rather than being solitary apostates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T13:36:14-08:00","id":813606,"title":"","content":"After running today alchemy-heavy game of mortal investigators, I got idea on the next needed change in the 2ED...<br /> <br /> <b>Uncrowned Kings</b> \u2013 <i>Moros, Silver Ladder or Free Council </i>\u2013 Alchemy is described as Royal Art not without reasons - many alchemists were working for kings and queens. Many others <b>were</b> royalty. What's more important is that alchemist worked to perfect themselves and world around them to create perfect state - physical, political and mental - and all those concepts reason with Silver Ladder philosophy. Adding clearly Elemental Precepts as base of Ladder dogma, it is wonder how in 1ED Coal-Burners were <i>not</i> this Order's Legacy. Still, Uncrowned Kings reason in modern times very much with chemistry and psychology, both connected more to Sleepers belives and technology - so being part of also Free Council have sense. <b>Knowledge needed:</b> Crafts 2, Occult 1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T08:05:48-08:00","id":814131,"title":"","content":"BTW, if you want some good inspiration for Uncrowned Kings, look for Jung's works on Alchemy and Psychology - it ficts perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T08:44:22-08:00","id":814154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=813606#post813606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After running today alchemy-heavy game of mortal investigators, I got idea on the next needed change in the 2ED...<br /> <br /> <b>Uncrowned Kings</b> \u2013 <i>Moros, Silver Ladder or Free Council </i>\u2013 Alchemy is described as Royal Art not without reasons - many alchemists were working for kings and queens. Many others <b>were</b> royalty. What's more important is that alchemist worked to perfect themselves and world around them to create perfect state - physical, political and mental - and all those concepts reason with Silver Ladder philosophy. Adding clearly Elemental Precepts as base of Ladder dogma, it is wonder how in 1ED Coal-Burners were <i>not</i> this Order's Legacy. Still, Uncrowned Kings reason in modern times very much with chemistry and psychology, both connected more to Sleepers belives and technology - so being part of also Free Council have sense. <b>Knowledge needed:</b> Crafts 2, Occult 1</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason they're in the FC is because they advocate ruler ship of the self, not of others. They're also hardline blue collar, learning about themselves through character building hard work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T09:17:05-08:00","id":814175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=814154#post814154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason they're in the FC is because they advocate ruler ship of the self, not of others. They're also hardline blue collar, learning about themselves through character building hard work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite - they strife to perfection, inter and outer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1ED corebook, Uncrowned Kings</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The truth behind those legends would shock the royal addicts who heard them. Indeed, the mages of Atlantis had learned the \u201ctrick\u201d of transmuting one substance into another, but it was only an incidental side effect of their real work. Their labors were not ultimately directed toward the external material world, but inward. <b>Like</b> <b>land, wood or stone, the human soul can be cultivated and shaped, they found, transformed into something both greater and finer than what it might otherwise be</b>. The \u201clead\u201d that they operated upon was themselves, and the \u201cgold\u201d that they created was themselves.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> Inheritors of this Legacy are known as the \u201cUncrowned Kings,\u201d a term that most outsiders take to refer to the age of the charlatans, when the<b> rulers of the world could be led by their vacuous desires and anyone who knew those desires could easily become a true \u201cpower behind the throne.\u201d</b> But a more esoteric meaning is hidden in the name. Having perfected the technique of crafting their own souls, the Uncrowned could truly claim to be \u201cself-made men,\u201d masters of their own souls. Their \u201croyalty\u201d is based, not upon primogeniture or the hoarding of hollow wealth, but upon the <b>noble qualities that they have cultivated within themselves</b>. They do not rule over nations, but over themselves to a degree that \u201ccommon\u201d folk can scarcely imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Silver Ladder</i> is not only about ruling Sleepers - it's their far reach plan. But perfecting on self and souls of others, practicing and mastering real Supernal Magic is viable way for them of working with Order dogma ( by Precepts of Thunder and Blood ). <i>Uncrowned Kings</i> perfects themselves, showing example for other they can be also. Making by products of material transmutation give them &quot;power behind the throne&quot; and they collect their &quot;noble qualities&quot; in their experiments. In mine book this sounds a lot like Ladder mages.<br /> <br /> Looking only on Legacy as <i>&quot;they make they hand dirty so they cannot be in Silver Ladder&quot;</i> is counter to Orders and offensive to the Tearchs point - their <b><i>whole Order </i></b>is based on <i>everlasting work of perfecting themselves and humanity</i>, laws and society to prepare people for Hieraconis. And some Silver Ladder offshots are more dedicated to the human perfection itself - just look over <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Clavicularius</i>, <i>Scions of God</i> or <i>Bene Ashmedai</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, I cannot imagine Silver Ladder would not try something that is described as <b>&quot;Royal Art&quot;</b>. In truth, even if I'm more self the Libertine, I was very </span></span>surprised that Uncrowned Kings were in <i>Free Council</i> in the first place. Then I read it was all based on their dedication to the craftsmanship - but then I thought &quot;What, they are only in the FC because it's technological Order?&quot; and still sound weird in mine head. I get that technology and modern psychology are more FC shtick, but this Legacy have <i>really</i> ancient roots.<br /> <br /> Then you go in to all the Hermetics and Rosicrucianism from 12 century onward and think &quot;Damn, it <i>does</i> sound a lot like Silver Ladder objectives&quot;. And you see there that one of most iconic Legacies incarnating those ideas is in Free Council? And that means it was:<br /> <br /> <i>A. Created in XIX century, even if Sleeper believes have at least one millenium on this subject - and this is not very plausible in <b>Mage</b> setting at large.</i><br /> or<br /> <i>B. Being Nameless for all those centuries, even if those occultism philosophies were practiced hard<br /> in this millenium at least and connected to the social circles of power, where Silver Ladder are having most foothold.</i><br /> <br /> It's just do not have logical sense, as Legacy and Orders history. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Much </b>more probable is that <i>Uncrowned Kings </i>were Moros and Silver Ladder Legacy by thousands of years, but in XIX century many of their most craftsmanship and science dedicated members described as Coal-Burners gone over to Nameless and newly forming Free Council, especially with the human innovations developments. And so, in 2ED you have <b>both </b>Silver Ladder and Free Council as parent Orders for Uncrowned Kings now. If <i>Eleventh Question</i> can have dual parent Orders, why <i>Kings</i> cannot have? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-06-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:27:35-08:00","id":814232,"title":"","content":"Nothing you said actually disagrees with my point, which was just an explanation of why they're in the FC. I don't care if you put them in the SL too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:53:10-08:00","id":814262,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as soon as the 2nd Edition book comes out I plan on updating a couple of the legacies, assuming that we don't have official versions of them. In particular I've been planning ideas on how to do the Reality Stalkers, House of Ariadne and the Stone Scribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:13:36-08:00","id":814283,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>, I honestly always felt that they were also appropriate within the Arrow as well. The idea of perfecting oneself through trials and hard work, and dismissing getting something from nothing, always seemed to be an extension of the core principles of the Arrow. Honestly, I think that a number of the Legacies can overlap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas#post805117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>The Quiescent </b>\u2013 <i>Moros and Guardians of Veil</i> \u2013 once again \u201cPath: Any\u201d group that should be just Guardians offshoot \u2013 well, maybe small Nameless Order on themselves. Ruling Arcana of Time and Optitonal as Death works for them. <b>Knowledge needed:</b> Science 1, Larceny 1 ( they want to pass magic as subtle tricks and new technology )</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I always felt that they were more of a FC themed legacy, as their decision to pursue the legacy and practice of &quot;Quiet Magic&quot; both arose from the changes of the sleeper world and a wish to remain integrated in it. In fact, I think that the point made that this is an &quot;any order&quot; legacy was a good one- All Orders would have reason to pursue the philosophy:<br /> -Guardians are obvious<br /> -The Ladder promotes Leadership by example, and subtle guidance could be appreciated.<br /> -Arrows may adopt it out of an understanding of protecting mortals from both themselves as well as others, since the sleeping curse harms others.<br /> -Mysterium seek to protect magic, and hiding it via the Quiet philosophy would do so<br /> <br /> But then, this goes to my above point: some Legacies can overlap with orders and paths, because their philosophies arise from specific focuses and time periods, which in turn are going to blend and mix the archtypes of the orders (as the more complicated and specific philosophies of legacies should).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:33:32-08:00","id":814308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=814283#post814283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I always felt that they were more of a FC themed legacy, as their decision to pursue the legacy and practice of &quot;Quiet Magic&quot; both arose from the changes of the sleeper world and a wish to remain integrated in it. In fact, I think that the point made that this is an &quot;any order&quot; legacy was a good one- All Orders would have reason to pursue the philosophy:<br /> -Guardians are obvious<br /> -The Ladder promotes Leadership by example, and subtle guidance could be appreciated.<br /> -Arrows may adopt it out of an understanding of protecting mortals from both themselves as well as others, since the sleeping curse harms others.<br /> -Mysterium seek to protect magic, and hiding it via the Quiet philosophy would do so<br /> <br /> But then, this goes to my above point: some Legacies can overlap with orders and paths, because their philosophies arise from specific focuses and time periods, which in turn are going to blend and mix the archtypes of the orders (as the more complicated and specific philosophies of legacies should).</div> </div> </div> </div>With Quiet it sounds as perfect example of Nameless Order thing - the Legacy description sounds as small club, with maybe a dozen mages worldwide, that come with their own philsophy, nothing clear connected to the Order on really reasonating idea. This &quot;Path: Any&quot; can mean they are Nameless Order and Legacy is needed to be teached by it's members - cause it's so entranched in Nameless philosophy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:43:14-08:00","id":814322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=814308#post814308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Quiet it sounds as perfect example of Nameless Order thing - the Legacy description sounds as small club, with maybe a dozen mages worldwide, that come with their own philsophy, nothing clear connected to the Order on really reasonating idea. This &quot;Path: Any&quot; can mean they are Nameless Order and Legacy is needed to be teached by it's members - cause it's so entranched in Nameless philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though I also feel that they somewhat transcend rather than sidestep Orders. Their philosophy is focused on the &quot;how&quot; of using magic, but in a very mechanical sense (prefer subtle versus overt/vulgar), and the reasoning doesn't really contradict any Order. An Arrow or Free Council member can still pursue his Orders values, they just does so without being flashy in their use of magic.<br /> <br /> I always see Nameless Orders as those whose philosophies either cannot fit within the Orders, would be rejected by the Orders, or who choose for tradition or pride to remain separate. Tremere are the classic example, as while some might hide within the Orders, no Order is going to overtly support them and their purpose is antithetical to not only Orders but the Paths themselves (destroy the 5 Watchtowers, raise their own from the Ouroboros/Abyss).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:02:20-08:00","id":814341,"title":"","content":"Any Legacies you guys think should change their Path ? I already said it in another topic but personally with the new path writeups I just can't fit the Blank Badges into Acanthus, they feel so much Mastigos for me that it hursts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:09:48-08:00","id":814351,"title":"","content":"I honestly always felt the 11th Question to fit the Obrimos well with 2e's Arcana previews, as with a Ruling Arcana of Prime (Truth) and inferior Arcana of Death (Secrets), the Obrimos Path seems like one where a legacy that seeks to uncover the truth would naturally be drawn into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:21:22-08:00","id":814365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=814341#post814341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Legacies you guys think should change their Path ? I already said it in another topic but personally with the new path writeups I just can't fit the Blank Badges into Acanthus, they feel so much Mastigos for me that it hursts</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagineers were...not well thought out. The FC book really got the shaft when it came to legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T13:22:54-08:00","id":814424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=814341#post814341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Legacies you guys think should change their Path ? I already said it in another topic but personally with the new path writeups I just can't fit the Blank Badges into Acanthus, they feel so much Mastigos for me that it hursts</div> </div> </div> </div>I can, seeing as <i>Blank Badges</i> are <b>The Invisibles</b> rip-off. All idea on Legacy is that they are sooo wierd and counter-culture to the normal society, they are omited by it. Just look on typical cabal of them.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://images2.fanpop.com/images/photos/6800000/Official-Vertigo-Wallpapers-vertigo-comics-6894234-1600-1200.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> There is also strong theme on Destiny favoring them in quasi-mythical combat oppression ( and characters fighting the weakness their it shows ) that I can see their Secondary Arcanum as being Fate easily. Not going over all &quot;ultimate conspiracy theory&quot; angle of series. <br /> <br /> They do not feel to me &quot;demonic&quot; - rather just really &quot;fae&quot; in atmosphere. Really weird fae, but fae non the less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T13:45:10-08:00","id":814432,"title":"","content":"Sphinxes, as i see them, are also a Guardian Legacy, seeing as how they would fit to the cult within that awaits the Hieromagus and choose to actively search for her through Fate and Minds lenses. Their path remains Mastigos, but i see them as both Myst. and GoV connected","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T13:53:45-08:00","id":814436,"title":"","content":"I've read the Invisibles. Noncoformity is kind of a Mastigos thing and the legacy is more about rebelion and transgression that about consequences of choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:35:07-08:00","id":822455,"title":"","content":"As to back to <b>The Quiescent</b> a bit...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=814322#post814322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, though I also feel that they somewhat transcend rather than sidestep Orders. Their philosophy is focused on the &quot;how&quot; of using magic, but in a very mechanical sense (prefer subtle versus overt/vulgar), and the reasoning doesn't really contradict any Order. An Arrow or Free Council member can still pursue his Orders values, they just does so without being flashy in their use of magic.<br /> <br /> I always see Nameless Orders as those whose philosophies either cannot fit within the Orders, would be rejected by the Orders, or who choose for tradition or pride to remain separate. Tremere are the classic example, as while some might hide within the Orders, no Order is going to overtly support them and their purpose is antithetical to not only Orders but the Paths themselves (destroy the 5 Watchtowers, raise their own from the Ouroboros/Abyss).</div> </div> </div> </div>You know that ANYONE can learn particular Legacy in 2ED? Original Path and Orders just have easier.<br /> <br /> Also, if we go with your take then Tamers of Elements need to be part of every Order instead of &quot;Path or Nameless&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:13:20-08:00","id":822531,"title":"","content":"Tamers -are- part of every Order. Read their section again.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah I'm pretty sure Freemind knows anyone can technically learn any legacy. It looks like you misunderstood him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T12:29:34-08:00","id":822611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=822531#post822531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tamers -are- part of every Order. Read their section again.</div> </div> </div> </div>From Path side - like you can find Obrimos Tamers of Fire in Arrow and Free Council because they still are Obrimos. But not every Arrow and Tearch can become Tamers of Fire, only Obrimos ones - because those practice are Nameless Order on to itself, eluding the Pentacle Orders teachings about normal magic.<br /> <br /> &quot;Original&quot; Path and Orders are <b><i>most</i></b> archetypical and history entwined factions that 2ED Legacies coming from - you <b>can</b> have Mastigos Arrow Eleventh Question mage, but he need to put a lot more effort in Legacy than Moros, Guardians or Mysterium members.<br /> <br /> Tamers of Elements are described in <b>Legacy: the Ancient</b> as Nameless Order onto itself - and should be that in 2ED, especially as it is great example of Nameless Legacy that <i>did not</i> become part of Free Council. All Pentacle Orders can have Tamers members as they all still can learn those Legacies by Path - but to learn those Arts from outside of Path, only Nameless can easily teach you - as they philosophy of Supernal is totally different than Pentacle Orders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=822531#post822531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, yeah I'm pretty sure Freemind knows anyone can technically learn any legacy. It looks like you misunderstood him.</div> </div> </div> </div>His post on <b>Quiescent </b>sounds a lot as he does not see this change. The Mage Noir makes <b>Quiescent</b> sound very much as Nameless Order in to itself - isolationist group of mages, with their own take on magic, somehow connected only vaguely on this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:10:37-08:00","id":822736,"title":"","content":"Direct quote from the book: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The tradition of the Tamers still crosses <b>paths</b> and orders today...They exist in their own right, and can be found among members of all <b>Paths</b> and orders. </div> </div> </div>Case in point? I'm pretty sure Aquila from Soul Cages is a Thyrsus, but also an Arrow and a member of the Tamers of Fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-03-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T20:22:34-08:00","id":823009,"title":"","content":"With 2ED Legacy rules <i>every</i> Legacy can be found in <i>every</i> Path and Order.<br /> <br /> It's still logical from inner groups teaching that Tamers stick to their original Paths and can be easily spread in Nameless community - they are just most common places new members to be found.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T21:25:24-08:00","id":823055,"title":"","content":"So, I originally had a much longer post, but I feel it's point may get lost and I am on call. Suffice it to say that Mrmdubois was right; Wyrd missed my point. I know anyone can learn a Legacy, regardless of Order or Path. <br /> <br /> My point was that you cannot conflate the idea that &quot;this legacy transcends path and/or order&quot; with &quot;this Legacy=Nameless Order.&quot; This may be the case for the Tamers and Tremere, but this doesn't mean all fit that model. All Legacies view magically differently as their shaping of their soul literally alters their ruling arcana and incorporates their legacies symbolism intro hero path; so simplynhaving a different take from the mainstream isn't itself a disqualification from being part of the Big 6.<br /> <br /> Most of the Legacies that do fall into being Nameless either are so drastically different that they either cannot fit into an Order or an Order would refuse them. Nameless Orders usually have some structure beyond &quot;connected vaguely&quot;: the Tremere are tied to the raising of an Abyssal (or something) Watchtower via the collection of souls due to a rather complicated philosophy concerning the nature of the soul, with Houses and a hierarchy. <br /> <br /> Some Legacies instead find roles in multiple Orders because their view is shared or can overlap. The 11Q originally arose from the focus of the Guardians on investigation, but their focus on the Truth has expanded past that, not because they are Nameless now.<br /> <br /> As I already acknolwedged, he Path and Order are Archtypes, but that is because those paths and Order have similar views to the Legacy, while others might contradict. The Perfected Adepts are stereotypically Obrimos as theory view Life as an energy that can be directed and controlled, which fits the classical Obrimos Path view and Mage Sight; the Adepts view on achieving perfection, challenging oneself, etc. all fold into the Arrows. It doesn't mean a Mastigos or a Seer Adept is impossible, just that their philosophy and take on magic may not be as readily accepted by those not coming from the associated path/order. And that there are occasional oddballs doesn't mean a particular Legacy isn't associated with a particular Path/Order because of this.<br /> <br /> For the Quiescent, they simply view that their role is to serve and guide, and magic is to be subtle; there is nothing indicating the intent to break away (though generally the Orders of that time are portrayed as didn't get the Legacy). Their world view wasn't incompatible with the Orders and their isolation was as much from one another, not an intentional withdrawal, in part just due to the nature of the Attainments. <br /> <br /> Essentially, I was arguing Quiescent are a inter-Order and Pathless group of like-minded mages who simply wanted magic to be kept hidden, rather than a separate Nameless Order or a Legacy tied to a specific Path.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I am on call, so I plan to re-read this when my brain is less addled so expect possible edits when I realize that I am rambling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T01:35:16-08:00","id":823158,"title":"","content":"<b>Note:</b> I use here often <b>Left Hand Path</b> that <b>DaveB </b>wrote and said it's material is most updated to 2ED standards of all 1ED <b>Mage</b> books, setting wise. I advise to read it anyone dwelling in to reinterpreting the Legacies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=823055#post823055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was that you cannot conflate the idea that &quot;this legacy transcends path and/or order&quot; with &quot;this Legacy=Nameless Order.&quot; This may be the case for the Tamers and Tremere, but this doesn't mean all fit that model. All Legacies view magically differently as their shaping of their soul literally alters their ruling arcana and incorporates their legacies symbolism intro hero path; so simplynhaving a different take from the mainstream isn't itself a disqualification from being part of the Big 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>And mine point you simply <b>cannot have this</b>. New rules are clear on this because 1ED was so vauge and in 1ED groups Legacy group could be anything that based it on soulshaping. In 2ED, Legacy is <u>Path's</u> group that sometimes resonate with greater Order or Nameless traditions, being spread by them. Tremere <i>are not</i> fundamentally Nameless group - they are, <b>first and for most</b>, Moros mages stealing souls and magic of others Legacies. Eleventh Question are <i>not</i> just some rundom &quot;detective mages&quot; - they <b>are</b> Moros bent on Time and uncovering riddles. Others Orders and Paths can join becuase, in the end, soulshaping is individual matter. <b>But each Legacy starts as off-shoot of Path.</b><br /> <br /> Just read the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/legacies/\" target=\"_blank\">Legacies spoiler</a>'s this sections:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legacies spoiler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Path, Order or Praxis:</b> All Legacies <b>possess an originating <u>Path</u></b>, and many (though not all) are connected to an Order\u2014Pentacle, Seer or Nameless.<br /> Normally, your mage must either belong to the Legacy\u2019s Path or Order. However, it is possible for a mage of any Path or Order to join a Legacy if she learns a Praxis that duplicates the Legacy\u2019s first Attainment, and utilizes one of the Legacy\u2019s Yantras. She develops the understanding to join without other requirements. If your character learns an Attainment duplicating a Praxis (whether she used it as an entry method or not) she receives an Experiences refund, with a bit extra, for the Praxis\u2019 cost. In this way, characters are encouraged to \u201ctrain\u201d for their future Legacies by specialising in the spells that will become Attainments, or develop their own Legacies out of their personal styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legacies spoiler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Optional Effect:</b> Some Legacy Attainments include an additional or alternate effect if the mage possesses dots in an additional Arcanum equal to the required Legacy Ruling Arcanum. This additional Arcanum is almost always a Ruling Arcanum from the Legacy\u2019s originating Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, 2ED Legacies are first and foremost the <b>tradition of Path's mages</b> - all other associations are second handed. That's why you <b><i>cannot </i></b>have group that is &quot;Pathless&quot;. Legacy is Path's group - plain and simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=823055#post823055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the Legacies that do fall into being Nameless either are so drastically different that they either cannot fit into an Order or an Order would refuse them. Nameless Orders usually have some structure beyond &quot;connected vaguely&quot;: the Tremere are tied to the raising of an Abyssal (or something) Watchtower via the collection of souls due to a rather complicated philosophy concerning the nature of the soul, with Houses and a hierarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not agree with this because - time and again - <b>DaveB</b> said that modern Pentacle Orders are made of subNameless Orders that agree to general line and slightly tweak their philosophy, joining alliance. EVERY Nameless can join, if he will be willing to slightly change his percepts. It's not &quot;all or nothing&quot; - some parts need to be cut out, but Orders are so varied because they are, in the end, super alliance of previous Nameless sects ( called Darshanas in <i>&quot;To the Strongest&quot;</i> from <b>Dark Eras</b> ). In the nutshell - <b>Pentacle is complex alliance of Nameless cults that sometime forget they are Nameless because of Atlantis rethorics \u2013 and over two thousands years of cooperation.</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And again <b>Left Hand Path</b> quote on the matter of what <i>are</i> Nameless:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Left Hand Path, p.36</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>We\u2019re All Alone Here: The Nameless Orders </b><br /> The orders and Ministries believe that apostates are contained, made safe by isolation and left to wallow in their own mistakes. They\u2019re wrong, and history should teach them better.<br /> Alternatives to the large sects have always existed. Before the Great Refusal, Nameless fraternities rivaling Seer Ministries in size spread across the globe, innovating new magical techniques and training their own apprentices. They became the great wild card in the war between Seer and Pentacle, and the Ministry of Hegemony\u2019s attempt to co-opt them led to the Free Council. Before they formed the fifth order of the Pentacle, the Diamond called these mages \u201cThe Nameless Orders,\u201d mocking them as rough associations of Nefandi, techgnostics, and other disreputable willworkers.<br /> Despite simplified histories taught to newly apprenticed Libertines, not every Nameless Order joined the Free Council or even took the opposite side to join the Pantechnicon Ministry. The Free Council was formed around alliances between the largest techgnostic Nameless Orders and absorbed free-thinking but non-Atlantean cults as the Great Refusal gathered pace. Those Nameless cults that disagreed with the Libertine creed declined the order status the Silver Ladder were offering to their cousins. Unwilling to fight the Seers or join the Pentacle, they vanished, scattering into component Cabals until it was safe to reestablish contact.<br /> In modern times, the Nameless orders (a term they now wear as a badge of pride) are loose alliances of apostate solitaries and cabals. Membership has only one requirement: a Nameless must not be a member of any other sect. Other than that, the Nameless grow organically out of cabal alliances \u2014 a group of Echo Walkers out of Tulsa might be given shelter by a bitter apostate with a grudge against the sentinels hunting them. Once the heat has died down, the Reapers move on\u2026 but they stay in touch. The old man now has friends who can teach him some unusual Life spells and debate the finer mechanisms of the human soul with him.<br /> Strange things breed in unnoticed places. The more an apostate interacts with the Nameless orders, the more he picks up a petri-dish of different magical styles and influences. Techniques and powers more organized mages wouldn\u2019t believe possible are his to command.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Orders cannot harbor groups like Tremere simply because the Liches are soul eaters and this is one of greatest sins mage can do. So Tremere inflitrate normal Pentacle society, just like characters can be part of two Orders ( see 1ED corebook on that ). In the end, Tremere are Nameless that walks inside Pentacle, with the strange philosophy they have, <i>not</i> proper part of Orders that would not let group like this survive in their midst consiesly.<br /> <br /> And now literal quote on Elemental Tamers matter from <b>Left Hand Path</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Left Hand Path, p.27</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interrelated \u201cElemental Tamer\u201d Legacies claim descent from the Barbarian Kingdoms of legend rather than Atlantis. Before the industrial revolution they made up the largest Nameless order. Since the Great Refusal, most of the surviving Legacies have found a place in the Pentacle, but some still find the alliance uncomfortable. The <b>Tamers of Blood</b> were once one of the most prominent Tamer sects. A Thyrsus Legacy specializing in Life and Space, the Tamers of Blood are famous for their talent with body control, but the Pentacle is more concerned with another side to their attainments. Legacy members have the ability to forge powerful sympathetic bonds between people by ritually comingling blood, can use their attainments on anyone they have bonded as easily as on themselves, and are accused of not disclosing the level of control this gives over their clients until it\u2019s too late. The Tamers remain trapped as neither loyalists nor apostates, drawn in toward the Pentacle by their more respectable cousins but keeping a wary distance in case they are declared Left-Handed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tamers are asimilated only on the base they share Paths with other Pentacle mages. Their &quot;Nameless Tradition&quot; is in contrast with Atlantis rethorics and Elemental manipulation is in contrast with mostly Mysterium lead theory of Supernal. That's why Elemental Tamers <b>are still</b> Nameless, even if it's over a century when they joined Pentacle. To be taught Tamers ways outside of Path, you need to have totally diffrent view on magic than what most Orders show. And in the end \u2013 non Order really can agree with them to \u201ctake care of\u201d them at large.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=823055#post823055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Legacies instead find roles in multiple Orders because their view is shared or can overlap. The 11Q originally arose from the focus of the Guardians on investigation, but their focus on the Truth has expanded past that, not because they are Nameless now.</div> </div> </div> </div>11th Questions were <i>never</i> a truly Nameless - they are XIX century Moros group originating from Guardians and Mysterium quarrels. They <b>always</b> being part of Diamond infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=823055#post823055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Quiescent, they simply view that their role is to serve and guide, and magic is to be subtle; there is nothing indicating the intent to break away (though generally the Orders of that time are portrayed as didn't get the Legacy). Their world view wasn't incompatible with the Orders and their isolation was as much from one another, not an intentional withdrawal, in part just due to the nature of the Attainments.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I was arguing Quiescent are a inter-Order and Pathless group of like-minded mages who simply wanted magic to be kept hidden, rather than a separate Nameless Order or a Legacy tied to a specific Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>But their history points they become small Nameless Order into itself\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Noir, p.22</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over the next few years, the three of them trained other mages in New York, Los Angeles, Chicago and Detroit in their philosophy. They inducted a few into the Legacy, once they were sure that the subject was ready to leave behind the quick power and flashy results that vulgar magic brought. Their philosophy and magical style, known as Quiet magic, proved more popular (and, obviously, easier to adopt than the Legacy), and other mages began spreading it. Entire Quiet cabals, known as \u201cWhispering\u201d or \u201cSotto Voce\u201d cabals, arose, but the Consilii to which they belong rarely had a sense of who they were or what they were doing. As such, <b>they gained a reputation as being untrustworthy, maybe even Seer plants. This, in turn, drove the Quiet mages even further from the mainstream of mage society.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Noir, p.23</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Orders:</b> Membership with the Quiescent is meant to be kept completely separate from order membership. Indeed, Liars are not supposed to identify themselves as such in any other context except as it related to Legacy study or business. As such, the Legacy includes members of all five orders. It could, in theory, even include Seers of the Throne, though it would take an exceptional mage to deceive a Liar long enough to join the Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their \u201csecret cell\u201d structure looks a lot like as Nameless Order inflitrating Pentacle Order. Does this looks like something familiar? Hmmm, let\u2019s think\u2026 <i>Teremere</i>! Quiescent have the same structure as Tremere \u2013 so if Tremere are originating as \u201cMoros or Nameless\u201d, Quiescent should also be Nameless.<br /> <br /> And as 2ED Legacy the need originating Path \u2013 as their Optional Arcanum is Death, Moros are natural choice. That\u2019s why I posit Quiescent as \u201cMoros or Nameless (Quiescent Order)\u201d Legacy for 2ED. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-04-2016, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T02:56:23-08:00","id":823190,"title":"","content":"You are still misinterpreting Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Pathless legacy doesn't mean that there isn't a predominant Path, it just means that the Mages of the originating Path don't keep it as Path intellectual property. They let anyone join. Case in point, Tremere will take anyone, so will the Quiescent, so will the Tamers hence Pathless.<br /> <br /> We are all well aware that it took a lot of Nameless cults joining together to make an Order. When they join an Order they lose their Nameless status though because they're in a NAMED Order. They might keep a private name for themselves, but that just makes them the Black Tower of the Adamantine Arrow. They're a faction. The groups that remain under the label Nameless are the ones that the Pentacle will not even attempt to assimilate. So yeah, the Tremere hide out in Mage society and try not to get caught but are part of a Nameless order. So what was your point other than belaboring the obvious?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 11th Questions were <i>never</i> a truley Nameless - they are XIX century Moros group originating from Guardians and Mysterium quarrels. They <b>always</b> being part of Diamond infrastructure. </div> </div> </div>Ok, here's an easy part you misinterpreted to correct, Freemind is saying that when the 11Q stopped being just Guardians and became Guardians and Mysterium that -didn't- suddenly make them Nameless. They're still part of the Pentacle. The reason he's bringing this up is because you seem to have the idea that if a legacy can be found in more than one Order then it somehow becomes Nameless. Which is false, and he's proving that to you. He wasn't saying the 11Q are Nameless. <br /> <br /> The only point you seem to have made that actually relates is that the Quiescent have adopted an organizational structure that's similar to the Tremere which could make them the equivalent of a modern Nameless order. Good job. I'd point out the dissimilarities though. The Quiescent don't leave their Orders, the Tremere actually do. They might maintain tangential ties to their old Order for purposes of infiltration, but for all intents and purposes the Tremere are another Order with their strict heirarchy, organization and ideology. The Quiescent and the Tamers are too individual to set up alternative systems that would resemble and Order and they're not completely rejected by the Orders so they don't become Nameless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T03:40:29-08:00","id":823205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=823190#post823190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pathless legacy doesn't mean that there isn't a predominant Path, it just means that the Mages of the originating Path don't keep it as Path intellectual property. They let anyone join. Case in point, Tremere will take anyone, so will the Quiescent, so will the Tamers hence Pathless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoiled rules directly oppose this interpretation - marked by my quotes from blog post point to this. We will need to see what's finally in 2ED corebook to resolve this dilemma.<br /> <br /> My own interpretation is that <i>Tremere</i> are still &quot;Originating: Moros&quot; mages - they just train anyone interested in their Legacy - as <i>anyone other</i> can be in any other Legacy with 2ED rules. If you can have Mastigos Silver Ladder as Perfected Adept character, you can have any Path <i>Tremere</i> - they just need to study hard, in contrast to Moros that &quot;just get it&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=823190#post823190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are all well aware that it took a lot of Nameless cults joining together to make an Order. When they join an Order they lose their Nameless status though because they're in a NAMED Order. They might keep a private name for themselves, but that just makes them the Black Tower of the Adamantine Arrow. They're a faction. The groups that remain under the label Nameless are the ones that the Pentacle will not even attempt to assimilate. So yeah, the Tremere hide out in Mage society and try not to get caught but are part of a Nameless order. So what was your point other than belaboring the obvious?</div> </div> </div> </div>That there is diffrence between once-Nameless-and-now-Orders-Faction and <i>Tremere</i>. Faction is so integreated in to Order that on first thought they are taken for just &quot;typical&quot; members - and Order at large is protecting them as part of group. Order is <b>promoting</b> them to those inside and outside - &quot;<i>Black Tower</i> is cool Arrwos guys, we approve them in our Order family&quot;. <i>Tremere</i> are so wierd heresy that even so large groups as Orders cannot reconcile their origin. <i>Tremere</i>, in truth, undermine almost everything that is &quot;Atlantean&quot; about Diamond. And the same can be said about <i>Tamers</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=823190#post823190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, here's an easy part you misinterpreted to correct, Freemind is saying that when the 11Q stopped being just Guardians and became Guardians and Mysterium that -didn't- suddenly make them Nameless. They're still part of the Pentacle. The reason he's bringing this up is because you seem to have the idea that if a legacy can be found in more than one Order then it somehow becomes Nameless. Which is false, and he's proving that to you. He wasn't saying the 11Q are Nameless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Khem, khem - maybe my English is so bad. Or pain killers I take from few days are making me bad sounding statements. But I was first to open the <i>Uncrowned Kings</i> to become &quot;Moros, Silver Ladder and Free Council&quot; Legacy, <b>not </b>pointing them as Nameless - they were part of Silver Ladder from the start. I really understand 2ED change that there could be multiple &quot;Originating&quot; Orders because of the history of particular Legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=813606#post813606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Much </b>more probable is that <i>Uncrowned Kings </i>were Moros and Silver Ladder Legacy by thousands of years, but in XIX century many of their most craftsmanship and science dedicated members described as Coal-Burners gone over to Nameless and newly forming Free Council, especially with the human innovations developments. And so, in 2ED you have <b>both</b> Silver Ladder and Free Council as parent Orders for Uncrowned Kings now. If <i>Eleventh Question</i> can have dual parent Orders, why <i>Kings</i> cannot have? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Now to your last point...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=823190#post823190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only point you seem to have made that actually relates is that the Quiescent have adopted an organizational structure that's similar to the Tremere which could make them the equivalent of a modern Nameless order. Good job. I'd point out the dissimilarities though. The Quiescent don't leave their Orders, the Tremere actually do. They might maintain tangential ties to their old Order for purposes of infiltration, but for all intents and purposes the Tremere are another Order with their strict heirarchy, organization and ideology. The Quiescent and the Tamers are too individual to set up alternative systems that would resemble and Order and they're not completely rejected by the Orders so they don't become Nameless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here I do not agree with you - <i>Quiescent</i> severe they ties to Orders on the same way <i>Tremere</i> does it. Yes, they nominally are part of it, but <b>Mage Noir</b> points they &quot;distance&quot; from it. <i>Tremere</i>, with their own alien philosophy, still are part of day to day life in Orders - Mysterium Tremere is still collector of knowledge for Atheneum, doesn't he? <i>Tremere</i> Arrow or Free Council are still first to fight.<br /> <br /> Yet still <i>Tremere</i> are treated as Nameless, for the point of philosophical affiliation for Legacy - even when most of their members are day to day members of Pentacle Orders life. And the same could be said about <i>Quiescent </i>and <i>Tamers.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-04-2016, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T05:12:56-08:00","id":823239,"title":"","content":"No, what's been spoiled doesn't contradict me, you're just misunderstanding the point I'm making. Yes, all legacies have a Path of origin. However, when members of that legacy go out of their way to recruit members from any Path then it can be considered Pathless. Not because it doesn't have a parent Path, but because Path is not important to initiation. I think basically we understand the same thing here, but we're having a disagreement on terminology.<br /> <br /> Tamers don't undermine the Atlantean mythos or they wouldn't be allowed into the Orders. They maintain a loose confederation which transcends Order, but it's not a strong enough bond or organization to be an alternative to an Order. Tremere on the other hand do have a strong enough allegiance and organization, as well as not being syncretized into the Orders that it is an alternative Order and due to size and lack of official recognition in any Order is considered Nameless.<br /> <br /> Great, then stop arguing that because Tamers and the Quiescent are transOrder they must be Nameless. They're not because they're officially recognized and accepted members of the Orders in which they're found.<br /> <br /> That paragraph is not saying that the Quiescent sever their ties to their Orders, it's saying that they don't mix legacy and Order business unless it's absolutely necessary. The Tremere on the other hand are forced to sever as many connections as possible and maintain only what's necessary to maintain a cover. Why? Because they're soul stealing! Mages notice that stuff and they're very, very good at solving whodunnit mysteries. It would be impossible for a Tremere to be active in his original Order and not get caught eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T05:27:27-08:00","id":823247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=823239#post823239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That paragraph is not saying that the Quiescent sever their ties to their Orders, it's saying that they don't mix legacy and Order business unless it's absolutely necessary. The Tremere on the other hand are forced to sever as many connections as possible and maintain only what's necessary to maintain a cover. Why? Because they're soul stealing! Mages notice that stuff and they're very, very good at solving whodunnit mysteries. It would be impossible for a Tremere to be active in his original Order and not get caught eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not agree with that, particular last statement, but this discussion I will move to other topic.<br /> <br /> Move along and post new Legacies update ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T08:05:00-08:00","id":823351,"title":"","content":"Just to chime in sense I still haven't left the hospital and thus can't touch a computer to read this/write a full response (plus I have been awake for 36+ hours and could be incoherent/unintentionally hostile):<br /> <br /> Mrmdubois summed up most of what my points were and covered them well. <br /> <br /> My point on Pathless was that there never seemed to be a Path preference in either recruitment or the view inherent to the Legacy, not that there was no Path of Origin. All Legacies are founded by mages, each mage has a Path, thus all Legacies originated from one Path or another. The Moros is as good as any for the original path of the Quiescent's founder, I just doubt based on their description that the founder ever limited to them or the Legacy philosophy/view was wholly dependent on the Moros Path.<br /> <br /> As for Orders, Mrmdubois hit most on the head. Nameless are mages not affiliated with or recognized as members of an Order, the Nameless Orders are associations of such groups. Groups that once were Nameless who joined with an Order lose the Nameless status. Association with multiple Orders just means that the Legacy found like minded individuals amongst more than one group. Just because a Legacy has an outside structure and hierarchy doesn't itself make them a separate Order, as long as the members actively work within and fulfill their roles within the Order(s); if having a heirachy or association beyond strict Order lines meant a Legacy became a separate Order then nearly all Legacies would technically fit the definition.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are Nameless because while they can come from or technicamy hold nominal affiliation with any of the Orders, they aren't themselves a part of them. As Mrmdubois pointed out, the recognize different goals, a separate heirarchy, and actively work to advanced the goals of the Tremere over their original/infiltrated Order, even if they still act along their Order's general goals. Remember, they are a group dedicated got he harvest of souls to undermine the entire basis of the Paths and Watchtowers by raising an alternative Tower (from possibly the Abyss) and destroying the originals; no Order would support this as it actively undermines the very basis of the known Supernal. And if discovered, the infiltrated Order would strip the Loch of their status and kill them. It is the same as if a Seer was to infiltrate a Pentacle Order, or vice versa. The Tremere aren't the model that describes other legacies; they are examples of how the Left Handed can operate as a cohesive organization and maintain themselves in the face of such overt opposition.<br /> <br /> My point was Quiescent don't hide their status; they (based on the text you quoted) simply don't place it above their Order, but alongside it. They might not be trusted, but they still work within their Orders goals and heirarchy, simply pursuing the use of subtle magic. Nothing about them expressly puts them outside the Orders except the general mistrust at that time for this new movement.<br /> <br /> Anyway... I need to get back to notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T19:22:14-08:00","id":824754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=823239#post823239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> . . .Tamers don't undermine the Atlantean mythos or they wouldn't be allowed into the Orders. They maintain a loose confederation which transcends Order, but it's not a strong enough bond or organization to be an alternative to an Order. Tremere on the other hand do have a strong enough allegiance and organization, as well as not being syncretized into the Orders that it is an alternative Order and due to size and lack of official recognition in any Order is considered Nameless. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on this a bit - if you look at <b>Legacies: the Ancient</b>, the Elemental Masteries (the formal &quot;umbrella&quot; name for all the different Tamer Legacies) actively <i>support</i> the Atlantean mythos. Modern adherents believe they're the heirs to the original Nameless, the barbarian mages who warred against the forces of Atlantis, back before the Fall. Heck, the Tamers of Rivers are <i>still </i>upset about the Watchtowers, preserving a half-remembered story about how the Atlanteans built them in a bid to keep the magic all to themselves.<br /> <br /> Being the enemy of Atlantis is not the same thing as undermining the Atlantean mythos. After all, its kind of hard to oppose a place that you don't believe ever existed. Instead, one needs to look more at Free Council Legacies such as the Blank Badges or the Roses of Eden - both of whom want to mulch the whole &quot;Atlantis&quot; idea to grow a better future.<br /> <br /> Now, the rotes and attainments of the Elemental Masteries are built on a different <i>paradigm</i> than traditional &quot;Atlantean&quot; magics, and an Atlantean-trained mage would have a hard time independently duplicating them . . . But the Diamond and the Tamers made peace long ago, and in the modern era there are plenty of Diamond Order mages who've been inducted into one of the Elemental Mastery Legacies - just as many Free Council mages practice various Atlantean-styles of magic. I suppose its a bit like the magical equivalent of being bilingual.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T22:48:01-08:00","id":824836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=824754#post824754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the rotes and attainments of the Elemental Masteries are built on a different <i>paradigm</i> than traditional &quot;Atlantean&quot; magics, and an Atlantean-trained mage would have a hard time independently duplicating them . . . But the Diamond and the Tamers made peace long ago, and in the modern era there are plenty of Diamond Order mages who've been inducted into one of the Elemental Mastery Legacies - just as many Free Council mages practice various Atlantean-styles of magic. I suppose its a bit like the magical equivalent of being bilingual.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this metaphor. But also I cannot fully support that &quot;Tamers weird philosophy = Free Council&quot;. Elemental Masteries were for MILLENIA outsiders to the Diamond. They were <i>in it</i>, but <b>rose an outer-Diamond culture on it's own</b>. See what <b>Legacies: The Ancient</b> have on this matter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legacies: The Ancient, p. 25</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gradual, inexorable rise of the Quiescence hit them hard. Paradoxes and Disbelief began to disrupt the works of these non-Atlantean mages, including the Tamers, and, unlike the Atlantean exiles, the Tamers had no organizations of their<br /> own to turn to. <b>Many tried to join with the Dragon Orders. </b><br /> <b>The Tamers were hardly met with open arms: the Atlanteans at best, patronized the Tamers, treating them as savages and peons.</b> At worst, the Atlanteans killed the Tamers out of hand. Some Atlanteans were unable to believe that Awakened mages could exist outside of the Dragon Orders, and considered these strange, \u201cuncivilized\u201d miracle-workers to be spies, or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legacies: The Ancient, p. 26</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Orders, Cabals and Signs</b><br /> <b>The Elemental Masteries are a distinct tradition. They exist in their own right</b>, and can be found among members of all Paths and orders. Certain of the Elementalists\u2019 Legacies are numerous among some orders more than others, but <b>the loose confederacy that comes from joining the Tamers spreads across the areas of magical society. </b><br /> Members of the Elemental Masteries often join together in cabals with other Tamers. Cabals wholly composed of Tamers are rare, particularly cabals representing all five Paths, but for centuries, tutors in each of the Elemental Masteries have encouraged their pupils to find other Tamers and to find common cause with them. As in any cabal, joining with others from different Paths and orders can prove a valuable learning experience, as well as a means of survival.<br /> <b>Traditionally, the practitioners of the Elemental Masteries were supposed to aid one another, regardless of any other affiliations.</b> During the last 200 years, the commitment of the Tamers to each other has eroded to the point that although lip service is paid to the principle, there really isn\u2019t any universally recognized obligation for the Tamers to offer help when asked.<br /> Still, given that most of the Tamers know how to recognize each other, there\u2019s a good chance that two Tamers who meet for the first time will be well disposed, at least initially, in much the same way that two Englishmen who meet by chance in a foreign country will strike up some sort of friendly conversation. Even if they have nothing else in common, it\u2019s a start.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legacies: The Ancient, p. 27</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Their powers are strikingly similar across the world; only the terms in which they express their magic differ from one culture\u2019s version of a Tamer to another. </b><br /> They are not the only Tamers in existence; they\u2019re simply the best known, and, in the case of the Tamers of Fire, Rivers, Stone and Winds, the most common. There are others. Some are limited in geographical scope. Others may not be quite as old. <b>But they are true Tamers, and although their powers might be esoteric in the extreme, they still recognize the same signs and same forms, and they still (mostly) bear an elemental mark on their nimbuses.</b><br /> Among the mages of the Far East, there are still rare examples of Tamers of Trees and Tamers of Iron, for example. Although few mages have met a Tamer of Ice or a Tamer of Rain, a few of each still apparently practice their works in regions covered by the former USSR. More elusive still are the Tamers of Light, who manipulate the very light of the sun, somewhere in South America, and the Tamers of Sand, who still practice their crafts in the remotest corners of the Australian Outback.<br /> Rumors still persist of (possibly Left-Handed) Tamers of Blood, but as far as most mages are concerned, if they ever existed, they\u2019re long gone now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too me, it's sounds a lot as global alliance of &quot;magical schools&quot; that is not Diamond or Seers and precedes the Free Council - Last I checked my books and <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/a-well-armed-society/\" target=\"_blank\">2ED society spoiler</a> that means <b>Tamers <i>are</i> Nameless Order</b>, are <i>text book definition of it</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Well Armed Society</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A </span></span></span><b>Nameless Order</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is one of any number of small, usually local or regional organizations of mages. Some belong to ancient magical traditions, while others consist of a handful of cabals who joined forces only a few years ago. Although a handful can wield considerable influence within their purview, they lack the global reach of the major Orders.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they are semi-allied with Pentacle, were working inside Diamond thousands of years before Free Council come to it - but they have still very distinct and universal culture. And I cannot see them as simple &quot;we are Free Council now&quot; - their tradition is much more older than that. Many Tamers can be Free Council, probably most are, but there are also those that are in Diamond and Seers.<br /> <br /> Plus, if their are &quot;<b>Originating:</b> Path or Nameless&quot; Legacy, it means that in their original cultures their Tradition can be taught to all Paths for people raised in those cultures - Tamers of Ice can be taught easily in any post-USSR country based on their folklore. Tamers of Light are so popular in South America myths that any Path can join.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T06:49:09-08:00","id":824921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=824836#post824836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this metaphor. But also I cannot fully support that &quot;Tamers weird philosophy = Free Council&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well good, because that's not what he said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T06:14:56-07:00","id":881711,"title":"","content":"Personally I never really thought the Tamers worked as &quot;heirs of the NonAtlantean Nameless&quot;. They're clearly rooted in a coherent cultural cosmology with the &quot;Atlantean&quot; (read: Greco-Indian) model of the elements and their Path Associations. The Tamers of the Cave are even specifically drawing on Plato!<br /> <br /> I'd have gone with someone like the Dreamspeakers for that role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T06:26:17-07:00","id":881721,"title":"","content":"Dreamspeakers are a non-Atlantean Nameless group as well. I doubt they've ever been organized enough to constitute a Nameless Order, but they'd be one of the groups that got, because of their Nameless status, drawn under the umbrella of the FC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:15:01-07:00","id":881939,"title":"","content":"I've always felt that the Sisterhood of the Blessed were a Mastigos Legacy, while the Reality Makers felt like an Acanthus Legacy. But that just might be me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:24:42-07:00","id":881951,"title":"","content":"No, you're probably right, Reality Makers being Mastigos never made any sense considering how far they'd have to stretch themselves to really own the legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:05:31-07:00","id":882210,"title":"","content":"I really, really want to make Prime / Death branch of Eleventh Question.<br /> But I'm too tired right now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:10:13-07:00","id":882216,"title":"","content":"Stone Scribes are a Legacy that record the Final Names of the deceased and take them on to steal their sympathetic connections. 1e had them as Moros with Fate; 2e says they're Moros with Time. Why wouldn't they have Space?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:17:25-07:00","id":882222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=882216#post882216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stone Scribes are a Legacy that record the Final Names of the deceased and take them on to steal their sympathetic connections. 1e had them as Moros with Fate; 2e says they're Moros with Time. Why wouldn't they have Space?</div> </div> </div> </div>Time is more with capturing &quot;photography&quot; of person - Remember what Time Arcanum does - it let you SEE the Past. Space would only point you in direction to where body is now - it's Time that freezes what person was - at least in Stone Scribes meaning.<br /> <br /> Of coures, they can have spell or two on Space as &quot;Legacy secret&quot; like many have - but most crutial for them is preserving &quot;memory&quot; of person after her death. Time sounds as perfect for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T18:08:25-07:00","id":882393,"title":"","content":"I just skimmed through this thread and didn't see this, has anyone had a chance to translate Brotherhood of the Demonwind yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11692-amseriah","name":"Amseriah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T00:44:34-07:00","id":882642,"title":"","content":"I'll have to translate Lords of the Inanimate for the Chronicle that's coming up. I think it'll be fairly easy though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T01:08:34-07:00","id":882657,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to figure out how to come at a 2e update for The Quiescent. Any ideas, now that vulgar magic is gone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T01:18:25-07:00","id":882665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solarious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=881939#post881939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always felt that the Sisterhood of the Blessed were a Mastigos Legacy, while the Reality Makers felt like an Acanthus Legacy. But that just might be me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My Reality Maker character was indeed Acanthus (Legacy access via her Silver Ladder membership). It played as being a glamour illusionist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T01:23:50-07:00","id":882669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=882657#post882657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to figure out how to come at a 2e update for The Quiescent. Any ideas, now that vulgar magic is gone?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They can still reject obvious magic as a philosophical principle without &quot;vulgar&quot; magic being a mechanical concept. The concept behind their Time Attainments still work fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T12:49:25-07:00","id":884830,"title":"","content":"Here is a rough, fluffless draft of a 2e version of the Bene Ashmedai. Let me know if anyone has any ideas for alternative effects for each Attainment.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Bene Ashmedai</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Special Rules:</b> Spirits affected by Bene Ashmedai Attainments must be of an emotional choir, having clear origins in human activity. Goetia may only be affected if they're from someone's Oneiros.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainment 1 </b><br /> Spirit 1: Exorcist's Eye [Applies to Goetia automatically if mage fulfils requirements]<br /> Mind 1: Know Nature<br /> <br /> <b>Attainment 2</b><br /> Spirit 2: Command Spirit [Applies to Goetia automatically if mage fulfills requirements]<br /> Mind 2: Psychic Domination [Limited to actions that fulfill the mage's Vice or Aspirations/Obsessions]<br /> <br /> <b>Attainment 3</b><br /> Spirit 3: Spirit Summons <br /> Mind 3: Goetic Summons<br /> <br /> <b>Attainment 4</b><br /> Spirit 4: Bind Spirit [Applies to Goetia automatically if mage fulfills requirements]<br /> Mind 4: Psychic Reprogramming [Limited to changes the ST feels would would make the subject fulfill the mage's Vice or Aspirations/Obsessions]<br /> <br /> <b>Attainment 5</b><br /> Spirit 5: Birth Spirit [Can replicate Psychic Genesis too if the mage fulfills requirements]<br /> Mind 5: Amorality [Can only remove someone's Virtue]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T13:50:16-07:00","id":884873,"title":"","content":"Remember that because of the way Reach is calculated for Legacy Attainments, each of the ones you made has only one Reach to spend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T13:59:38-07:00","id":884887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=884873#post884873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that because of the way Reach is calculated for Legacy Attainments, each of the ones you made has only one Reach to spend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're trying to tell me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:15:47-07:00","id":884895,"title":"","content":"I'm referring to the &quot;Fixed Reach&quot; rule on page 198. Because of it, your &quot;Psychic Domination&quot; Attainment allows you to spend only one Reach on the spell. In practice, the Bene Ashmedai can instantly make simple commands with a touch, but can't ask anyone to shoot themselves (which normally costs +2 Reach), even at Mind 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:39:45-07:00","id":884918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=884895#post884895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm referring to the &quot;Fixed Reach&quot; rule on page 198. Because of it, your &quot;Psychic Domination&quot; Attainment allows you to spend only one Reach on the spell. In practice, the Bene Ashmedai can instantly make simple commands with a touch, but can't ask anyone to shoot themselves (which normally costs +2 Reach), even at Mind 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>False. Fixed Reach means you cannot exceed your 'safe Reaching' limit for the effect by risking Paradox, not that you are stuck at the Reach amounts available for the specific level of Arcana the Attainment fits under-<br /> <br /> *rereads that section*<br /> <br /> Oh crap, you're right. That's... a bummer. I'm not sure how to design Attainments worth taking for this Legacy, now.<br /> <br /> Then again, maybe having someone be unable to kill themselves with that Attainment is a feature instead of a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 05-07-2016, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:22:42-07:00","id":884983,"title":"","content":"On the bright side, use of an attainment is almost always an Instant Action so you don't have to worry about wasting your Reach on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:25:22-07:00","id":884984,"title":"","content":"It is a bummer. I've been struggling with a Legacy of my own and I'm still not satisfied with it.<br /> <br /> I agree that mind-control doesn't seem to fit the Legacy. They are manipulators but nor slavers, and in the 1st Edition they felt responsibility towards Mortals. Still, if you made &quot;Psychic Domination&quot; the fifth Attainment, that would have been some scary stuff. Purple Man scary.<br /> <br /> When it comes to designing Attainments, it helps if you have a good grasp on what the Legacy does. Try to think on what exactly you think their self-avowed purpose is, and which Spells fit most. As far as Mind is concerned, I think they're:<br /> &quot;Know Nature&quot; - a 1 dot Spell as the 1st Attainment, with +1 free reach. Versatile and useful.<br /> &quot;First Impressions&quot; - a 2 dot Spell as the 2nd Attainment. I'm not clear on how to crunch the numbers, but I think a personal bonus to Social Maneuvering is the right fit.<br /> &quot;Mental Shield&quot; - a 2 dot Spell as the 3rd Attainment, with +2 free Reach. It allows you to protect both yourself and others, from all sorts of influences.<br /> &quot;Goetic Summons&quot; - a 3 dot Spell I'm not sure how to calibrate. 5th Attainment? Having a helpful Vice Demons would be a high level Attainment, even if we limit the Spell to Mage's personal ones. The Mage would probably still need to negotiate, as opposed to command, which fits the theme of the Legacy. Spirit 2 keeps them Materialized which is perfect.<br /> &quot;Amorality&quot; - a 5 dot Spell I'm not sure what to do with. The Virtue severing effect is frankly underwhelming, when used on oneself. Using it on others seems like a breach of conduct. If we use it for the 4th Attainment, it needs to be bundled with an additional effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:25:49-07:00","id":884985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=884983#post884983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the bright side, use of an attainment is almost always an Instant Action so you don't have to worry about wasting your Reach on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually helps a lot, yes.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of replacing the optional Mind effect on the 4th attainment with Familiar, to get some of that 'ally of demons' thing going stronger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:28:12-07:00","id":884986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=884984#post884984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a bummer. I've been struggling with a Legacy of my own and I'm still not satisfied with it.<br /> <br /> I agree that mind-control doesn't seem to fit the Legacy. They are manipulators but nor slavers, and in the 1st Edition they felt responsibility towards Mortals. Still, if you made &quot;Psychic Domination&quot; the fifth Attainment, that would have been some scary stuff. Purple Man scary.<br /> <br /> When it comes to designing Attainments, it helps if you have a good grasp on what the Legacy does. Try to think on what exactly you think their self-avowed purpose is, and which Spells fit most. As far as Mind is concerned, I think they're:<br /> &quot;Know Nature&quot; - a 1 dot Spell as the 1st Attainment, with +1 free reach. Versatile and useful.<br /> &quot;First Impressions&quot; - a 2 dot Spell as the 2nd Attainment. I'm not clear on how to crunch the numbers, but I think a personal bonus to Social Maneuvering is the right fit.<br /> &quot;Mental Shield&quot; - a 2 dot Spell as the 3rd Attainment, with +2 free Reach. It allows you to protect both yourself and others, from all sorts of influences.<br /> &quot;Goetic Summons&quot; - a 3 dot Spell I'm not sure how to calibrate. 5th Attainment? Having a helpful Vice Demons would be a high level Attainment, even if we limit the Spell to Mage's personal ones. The Mage would probably still need to negotiate, as opposed to command, which fits the theme of the Legacy. Spirit 2 keeps them Materialized which is perfect.<br /> &quot;Amorality&quot; - a 5 dot Spell I'm not sure what to do with. The Virtue severing effect is frankly underwhelming, when used on oneself. Using it on others seems like a breach of conduct. If we use it for the 4th Attainment, it needs to be bundled with an additional effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I'll consider these suggestions when I have some more time and see what I come up with!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:30:12-07:00","id":884989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=884983#post884983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the bright side, use of an attainment is almost always an Instant Action so you don't have to worry about wasting your Reach on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kind of worried about that. If you check the page 201 to read the &quot;Unobvious Answer&quot; Attainment, you'll see that it deliberately affixes +1 Reach to instant use. I don't think that Reach was a freebie","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:31:41-07:00","id":884991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=884984#post884984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a bummer. I've been struggling with a Legacy of my own and I'm still not satisfied with it.<br /> <br /> I agree that mind-control doesn't seem to fit the Legacy. They are manipulators but nor slavers, and in the 1st Edition they felt responsibility towards Mortals. Still, if you made &quot;Psychic Domination&quot; the fifth Attainment, that would have been some scary stuff. Purple Man scary.<br /> <br /> When it comes to designing Attainments, it helps if you have a good grasp on what the Legacy does. Try to think on what exactly you think their self-avowed purpose is, and which Spells fit most. As far as Mind is concerned, I think they're:<br /> &quot;Know Nature&quot; - a 1 dot Spell as the 1st Attainment, with +1 free reach. Versatile and useful.<br /> &quot;First Impressions&quot; - a 2 dot Spell as the 2nd Attainment. I'm not clear on how to crunch the numbers, but I think a personal bonus to Social Maneuvering is the right fit.<br /> &quot;Mental Shield&quot; - a 2 dot Spell as the 3rd Attainment, with +2 free Reach. It allows you to protect both yourself and others, from all sorts of influences.<br /> &quot;Goetic Summons&quot; - a 3 dot Spell I'm not sure how to calibrate. 5th Attainment? Having a helpful Vice Demons would be a high level Attainment, even if we limit the Spell to Mage's personal ones. The Mage would probably still need to negotiate, as opposed to command, which fits the theme of the Legacy. Spirit 2 keeps them Materialized which is perfect.<br /> &quot;Amorality&quot; - a 5 dot Spell I'm not sure what to do with. The Virtue severing effect is frankly underwhelming, when used on oneself. Using it on others seems like a breach of conduct. If we use it for the 4th Attainment, it needs to be bundled with an additional effect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Attainments should match dot levels, so your 3rd attainment ought to be better than a 2 dot effect and your 4th attainment can't be a 5th dot effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:33:57-07:00","id":884994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=884989#post884989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of worried about that. If you check the page 201 to read the &quot;Unobvious Answer&quot; Attainment, you'll see that it deliberately affixes +1 Reach to instant use. I don't think that Reach was a freebie</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Automatic Activation: In most cases, a Legacy Attainment can be activated with an instant action and does not require dice rolls. 2e Corebook pg. 198.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:34:33-07:00","id":884995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=884989#post884989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of worried about that. If you check the page 201 to read the &quot;Unobvious Answer&quot; Attainment, you'll see that it deliberately affixes +1 Reach to instant use. I don't think that Reach was a freebie</div> </div> </div> </div>But, the rules for Legacy Attainments are clear. It's always an instant action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:35:04-07:00","id":884996,"title":"","content":"That's what I've been banging my head against for the last few hours. <br /> <br /> This is what the section on Automatic Activation says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless specified otherwise, activating an Attainment is an instant action. </div> </div> </div>This is what the section on Reach says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Attainments use one Reach for instant \u201ccasting\u201d; those that don\u2019t (being based on ritual spells) take one scene of preparation to use. </div> </div> </div>The most logical interpretation of the text is that, when you design a Legacy Attainment, you lock the Reach in place and can't change it again. Most Legacy Attainments just use their one Reach for instant casting. <br /> <br /> In fact, most of the Eleventh Question Attainments specifically point out what their Reach is assigned to, and instant activation isn't free. That wasn't in the original preview, and since I skimmed most of the text that had already been posted on the blog, I didn't notice until now. <br /> <br /> That's going to have a huge affect on how Legacies are designed. You're more likely to see low-level spells adapted to high-level Attainments so they can get the extra Reach, and you're probably going to have problems finding appropriate spells for low-level attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:35:48-07:00","id":884997,"title":"","content":"Page 198<br /> &quot;For example, a two-dot spell that becomes a three-dot Attainment should be designed as if it automatically has +2 Reach, even if the user actually has four dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Eleventh Question use &quot;Postcognition&quot; (a 1 dot Spell) as the second Attainment.<br /> <br /> Edit: Awww, Ninja'd!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 05-07-2016, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:54:48-07:00","id":885012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=884996#post884996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I've been banging my head against for the last few hours.<br /> <br /> This is what the section on Automatic Activation says:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is what the section on Reach says:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The most logical interpretation of the text is that, when you design a Legacy Attainment, you lock the Reach in place and can't change it again. Most Legacy Attainments just use their one Reach for instant casting.<br /> <br /> In fact, most of the Eleventh Question Attainments specifically point out what their Reach is assigned to, and instant activation isn't free. That wasn't in the original preview, and since I skimmed most of the text that had already been posted on the blog, I didn't notice until now.<br /> <br /> That's going to have a huge affect on how Legacies are designed. You're more likely to see low-level spells adapted to high-level Attainments so they can get the extra Reach, and you're probably going to have problems finding appropriate spells for low-level attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>That looks like a contradiction that should be mentioned in the Errata thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:17:22-07:00","id":885023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=885012#post885012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That looks like a contradiction that should be mentioned in the Errata thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I already pointed it out. I figure it'll be added to the FAQ if it's not a mistake. <br /> <br /> I don't think it's necessarily a massive nerf, but it does make some things a lot more complicated. <br /> <br /> Say you want to convert the Reality Stalkers. Their attainments are very straightforward and most of them are converted or easy to figure out. <br /> <br /> First Attainment<br /> Space: Spatial Awareness<br /> Mind: ????<br /> <br /> Second Attainment<br /> Space: Scrying<br /> Mind: Incognito Presence<br /> <br /> Third Attainment<br /> Space: Co-Location<br /> Mind: Imposter<br /> <br /> Fourth Attainment:<br /> Space: ????<br /> Mind: Hallucination. It's not quite a perfect fit, but it's close enough. <br /> <br /> Fifth Attainment:<br /> Space: Pocket Dimension<br /> Mind: ????<br /> <br /> On the surface, you just need to account for the fact that Legacies now have five Attainments, and that Pocket Dimension is Space 5 rather than Space 4. <br /> <br /> But if you look at Reach, it doesn't work.<br /> <br /> On the Space side, Spatial Awareness is going to have a Duration in turns, although that might not be a major problem, Scrying won't do anything because it won't have enough Reach for a sensory effect, and Co-Location will only affect spaces you can touch. Only Pocket Dimension will work fine since you don't really need to cast that one instantly. On the Mind side, Incognito Presence, Imposter and Hallucination will only work at touch range, and their Duration is going to be in turns. In order to fix the problem you'll have to move the Attainments up. <br /> <br /> First Attainment:<br /> Space: ????<br /> Mind: ????<br /> <br /> Second Attainment:<br /> Space: Spatial Awareness<br /> Mind: ????<br /> <br /> Third Attainment:<br /> Space: Scrying<br /> Mind: Incognito Presence<br /> <br /> Fourth Attainment:<br /> Space: Co-Location<br /> Mind: Imposter<br /> <br /> Fifth Attainment:<br /> Space: Pocket Dimension<br /> Mind: Hallucination<br /> <br /> At the upper end, it works better since your Fourth Space and Fifth Mind Attainments are filled out, but you need to find new spells that are still useful if you have only one reach to spend in order to fill out the first two Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:26:29-07:00","id":885028,"title":"","content":"You can always add some non-spell perk or pick a lower level spell; lower level spells at higher attainments get more reach and are beefier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:58:55-07:00","id":885078,"title":"","content":"I managed to finish a conversion of the Tamers of Fire Legacy. I'm still missing Yantras for them, though. So, if anyone has some suggestions, that would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T22:23:18-07:00","id":885165,"title":"","content":"Behold, version two! Or is it three, since it's the second version of an adaptation of an original?<br /> <br /> <b>Bene Ashmedai</b><br /> <br /> Origins<br /> Parentage: Mastigos, Seers of the Throne or Silver Ladder<br /> Nickname: Diabolists<br /> Background: see Silver Ladder, pg. 58<br /> Appearance: see Silver Ladder, pg. 57<br /> <br /> Doctrine<br /> Prerequisites: Spirit 2, Empathy 2, and one of the following skills at 2 dots or higher: Expression, Occult, Persuasion, Socialize, or Subterfuge<br /> Initiation: The prospective Diabolist must make a mutually beneficial arrangement with the Goetic demon of their Vice under the observation of her tutor.<br /> Organization: The Bene Ashmedai have learned that gathering in numbers worries mages who aren't part of their Legacy due to their kinship with humanity's inner demons. Egotism doesn't help much with that either. As such, Diabolists do not often gather in numbers larger than mentor/student pairings, and otherwise remain aloof of their fellows.<br /> Theory: Weakness comes from denying the self and its desires. Bene Ashmedai give form to their desires as demons, and make common cause with them. They find power and pleasure both in this alliance, and by the process of perfecting it seek the ultimate form of both - Ascension.<br /> <br /> Magic<br /> Ruling Arcanum: Spirit<br /> Yantras: Succeeding in a Social Maneuvering roll against a spell's target without magic before the spell (+2), fulfilling your Vice (+1) or Obsession (+2) as part of the spell, making use of pentagrams or ritual circles as part of the spell (+1; +2 if they take at least a scene to implement), monologuing about the motives and desires of the spell's subject (+1; +2 if you talk about your own and make yourself vulnerable)<br /> Oblations: Acting as a guru or other spiritual authority; conversing with goetia or other goeticists; demonological research; engaging in a seduction (either as the initiator or as the pursued); giving in to Vice without concern for the consequences (or inspiring another to do so); indulging in the fear and/or adulation of others; learning another person\u2019s Virtue, Vice, or magical Obsession.<br /> <br /> Attainment 1<br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> Exorcist's Eye [Applies to Goetia automatically if mage fulfils requirements]<br /> Optional Mind 1<br /> Know Nature<br /> <br /> Attainment 2<br /> Prerequisites: Spirit 2, Empathy 3<br /> Channel Essence [Applies to Goetia automatically if mage fulfills requirements]<br /> Optional: Mind 2<br /> First Impressions<br /> <br /> Attainment 3<br /> Prerequisites: Spirit 3. In addition to the Empathy 3 requirement from the previous Attainment, the Diabolist must increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 3, or must attain two dots in a second skill from the list of possible requirements.<br /> Gossamer Touch [Applies to Goetia automatically if mage fulfills requirements]<br /> Optional Mind 3<br /> Mental Shield<br /> <br /> Attainment 4<br /> Prerequisites: Spirit 4, Empathy 4, and the other Skill requirements of the previous Attainment.<br /> Bind Spirit [Applies to Goetia automatically if mage fulfills requirements]<br /> Optional Mind 4<br /> Goetic Summons [Can be Materialized if the mage desires it]<br /> <br /> Attainment 5<br /> Prerequisites: Spirit 5. In addition to the Empathy 4 requirement from the previous Attainment, the Diabolist must increase the other Skill she used to meet the requirements of the Legacy to 4, or must attain three dots in a second Skill from the list of possible requirements, or two dots in a third Skill from the list.<br /> Banishment [Applies to Goetia automatically if mage fulfills requirements]<br /> Optional Mind 5<br /> Amorality [Can only remove the subject's Virtue, but makes them Open to any ephemeral entity with a strong tie to their Vice]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 05-08-2016, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T23:08:06-07:00","id":885193,"title":"","content":"How about my favorite Summoners Legacy?<br /> <br /> <b>Choir of Hashmallim</b>: <i>Obrimos and Adamantine Arrow. </i>As might be obvious, a wandering group of Abyss hunters whose attainments revolve around building a relationship with a Supernal lieutenant to help them burn away the Void is based around the ideas of conflict as a mystical praxis-the True and Logical against the False and Incomprehensible. Attainments revolve around making it harder for the Abyss to fight the Aetherial Avatar, and making the Aetherial Avatar ever stronger in its mission. Probably should have more broad focus than just the Abyss, though-maybe a bonus to Scrutiny rolls to detect the ultimate origin of an effect is a middle-ranking Attainment. Main Arcanum is Spirit. <b>Knowledge Needed: </b>Occult 2, one of the Attack Skills (Weaponry, Brawl, Athletics) 1, must help banish a Gulmoth during initiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T23:18:36-07:00","id":885200,"title":"","content":"As Choir is one of important groups in my game I will talk about it a bit...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=885193#post885193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about my favorite Summoners Legacy?<br /> <br /> <b>Choir of Hashmallim</b>: <i>Obrimos and Adamantine Arrow. </i><br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> Main Arcanum is Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where are you with that and could work with this - only there is one little thing - it's SUMMONERS Legacy.<br /> <br /> It's whole concept is based on summoning ANGELS - and Angels can be summon only by Obrimos, using their Path Ruling Arcana. You cannot change Arcanum because it won't be then <i>Choir </i>as it is shown in <b>Summoners</b>.<br /> <br /> I can point you to <i>Eyes of Ein Soph </i>- they are Spirit based legacy of Obrimos looking for imperfections in reality. Not Abyss hunters per se, but even I choose them for Civitas Legacy for helping him finding taints in reality around him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T23:26:30-07:00","id":885204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=885200#post885200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Choir is one of important groups in my game I will talk about it a bit...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I can see where are you with that and could work with this - only there is one little thing - it's SUMMONERS Legacy.<br /> <br /> It's whole concept is based on summoning ANGELS - and Angels can be summon only by Obrimos, using their Path Ruling Arcana. You cannot change Arcanum because it won't be then <i>Choir </i>as it is shown in <b>Summoners</b>.<br /> <br /> I can point you to <i>Eyes of Ein Soph </i>- they are Spirit based legacy of Obrimos looking for imperfections in reality. Not Abyss hunters per se, but even I choose them for Civitas Legacy for helping him finding taints in reality around him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, but actually I already considered that.<br /> <br /> Truth is, I would have their primary Arcanum as Prime, but I'm not sure if a Legacy's favored Path Ruling Arcanum can be. As it is, Spirit is working, in that Spirit is the Arcanum of the instinctive minds inside of the world. The idea is that by helping their Avatar match the world's spirits, the Dominions can make it easier for the Avatar to stick around for long and frequent periods of time-as well as discovering when a &quot;spirit's&quot; makeup is actually impossible by any sane law of the world, instead being a Gulmoth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T23:29:44-07:00","id":885207,"title":"","content":"I kind of feel like we need some clarity around legacies in general. When is a buffed lower practice applicable, how do we balance higher arcana at higher legacy initiations etc?<br /> <br /> For me right now, Wraiths of Epochs are screwed. Primary attainments involve better post cog which could probably be described by more Reach. Optional attainments are kind of across the map. Especially the one that lets them pull stuff out of the past. It seems unnecessary to make that &quot;equipment&quot; so fragile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T23:57:50-07:00","id":885219,"title":"","content":"I think that Attainments should use Arcanum dots of Attainment level as Reach. This way:<br /> <br /> 1st - Instant casting or 1 Reach variant.<br /> 2nd - Instant casting + 1 Reach or 2 Reach variant.<br /> 3rd - Instant casting + 2 Reach or 3 Reach variant.<br /> 4th - Instant casting + 3 Reach or 4 Reach variant.<br /> 5th - Instant casting + 4 Reach or 5 Reach variant.<br /> <br /> Remember, we talk here about 4th and 5th powers that are at Gnosis 6 and 8 possible - higher safe Reaches then is not power problem. And they should have some incentive even, to make dwelling in Legacy worthwhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T00:11:39-07:00","id":885223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=885219#post885219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Attainments should use Arcanum dots of Attainment level as Reach. This way:<br /> <br /> 1st - Instant casting or 1 Reach variant.<br /> 2nd - Instant casting + 1 Reach or 2 Reach variant.<br /> 3rd - Instant casting + 2 Reach or 3 Reach variant.<br /> 4th - Instant casting + 3 Reach or 4 Reach variant.<br /> 5th - Instant casting + 4 Reach or 5 Reach variant.<br /> <br /> Remember, we talk here about 4th and 5th powers that are at Gnosis 6 and 8 possible - higher safe Reaches then is not power problem. And they should have some incentive even, to make dwelling in Legacy worthwhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like this setup for handling Reach with Legacy Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T06:29:58-07:00","id":885335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=885219#post885219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Attainments should use Arcanum dots of Attainment level as Reach. This way:<br /> <br /> 1st - Instant casting or 1 Reach variant.<br /> 2nd - Instant casting + 1 Reach or 2 Reach variant.<br /> 3rd - Instant casting + 2 Reach or 3 Reach variant.<br /> 4th - Instant casting + 3 Reach or 4 Reach variant.<br /> 5th - Instant casting + 4 Reach or 5 Reach variant.<br /> <br /> Remember, we talk here about 4th and 5th powers that are at Gnosis 6 and 8 possible - higher safe Reaches then is not power problem. And they should have some incentive even, to make dwelling in Legacy worthwhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that doesn't work. Initiate-level Attainments will still be useless since they'll only have one Reach, while Master-level affects will have significantly more Reach than comparable spells would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T07:21:42-07:00","id":885360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=885335#post885335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that doesn't work. Initiate-level Attainments will still be useless since they'll only have one Reach, while Master-level affects will have significantly more Reach than comparable spells would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. What if (most) Attainments are generally considered Instant Actions? That way, you can free up Reach for other effects, just as you can remove the Instant benefit to turn it into something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T08:06:53-07:00","id":885380,"title":"","content":"Move discussion about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885225-2e-errata-needed-problem-with-legacies-attainments-as-written\">Attainment Reach system problem to the topic we separated</a> - more will posts be there on problem, the more it will be seen as real problem with system and higher chances devs will fix it in Errata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T10:04:23-07:00","id":885452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=885335#post885335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that doesn't work. Initiate-level Attainments will still be useless since they'll only have one Reach, while Master-level affects will have significantly more Reach than comparable spells would.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe give them free Reach based on the same way Spells do from Arcana dots, but with Attainments instead? Probably not, but I felt it needed to be suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:52:11-07:00","id":887692,"title":"","content":"And I just realized that I kinda-sorta posted this in the wrong thread, so I'm reposting it here.<br /> <br /> I decided to try converting the Sphinxes to 2nd edition to see what would happen. My first observation is that the Sphinx Attainments are a lot wordier than the Mage 2nd Attainments. There are a lot of specifics, exceptions, and hedge cases that make it more complicated than it needs to be, and it really makes me appreciate Mage 2nd's standardized approach. Beyond that, it seems my suspicions that Fixed Reach was the best possible design decision was correct; it's much easier to choose Attainments when you can add or remove Reach to move spells around. I also added some commentary about my thought process in case it'd be useful. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Sphinxes</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>First Attainment: Surface Reading</b><br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> <br /> The Sphinx becomes attuned to the patterns that emerge within the Fallen World. This Attainment mimics the effects of Quantum Flux (p. 135). However, the Sphinx can only &quot;aim&quot; actions meant to solve puzzles, riddles, conundrums, or similar problems. This Attainment spends one Reach for instant activation.<br /> <br /> Optional: Mind 1<br /> <br /> After examining a subject for one scene, the Sphinx may learn information about the subject's thoughts. This functions as Mental Scan (p. 159). This Attainment's reach is spent on sensory range. </div> </div> </div>These were easy choices. Quantum Flux allows a Mage to quickly gain a short burst of contextual knowledge relevant a situation and accordingly, while Mental Scan effectively allows a Mage to read someone's body language in order to learn more about them. One focuses on the instinctual knowledge of the Sphinx Legacy, while the other focuses on their careful study of meaning. I find it strikes a nice balance. Allowing Sphinxes to &quot;aim&quot; actions related to riddles and gain Quantum Flux's benefit to solve riddles is a reference to the +3 bonus they got on Mental Skill rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Second Attainment: Hidden Meaning</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 2, Investigation 2<br /> <br /> The Sphinx becomes aware of the connections between people and objects. This Attainment replicates the effects of Interconnections (p. 134). Its Reach is spent on Advanced Duration and instant activation.<br /> <br /> Optional: Mind 2<br /> <br /> When using the optional effect of her first Attainment, the Sphinx also learns information revealed by Know Nature (p. 159). Reach is spent to reveal Aspirations and Obsessions and to use the Attainment at sensory range. </div> </div> </div>Interconnections was part of the Sphinx's original Attainments, so it was an obvious choice. Thematically, it broadens the scope of the Quantum Flux effect and allows Sphinxes to make broader connections between an immediate context and the rest of the world. Likewise, Know Nature builds upon the effects of Mental Scan. I hesitated about whether or not Know Nature and Mental Scan should be combined effects, but it was a much more elegant solution than keeping them separate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Third Attainment: The Leading Answer</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 3, Investigation 3<br /> <br /> The Sphinx may activate this Attainment in order to grant herself the benefits of Exceptional Luck (p. 135). The Sphinx may only use this Attainment on herself and may only grant herself boons. This Attainment's Reach is spent on instant activation and Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> Optional: Mind 3<br /> <br /> After studying someone with the optional effects of the firs two Attainments, the Sphinx gains the benefits of First Impressions (p. 160) towards the subject of her observations. This Attainment's Reach is spent on sensory activation and Advanced Duration. Once its duration expires, the Sphinx must examine her subject once more in order to update her profile and reactivate the Attainment. </div> </div> </div>Exceptional Luck was part of the Sphinx Attainments, but my initial choice for this was actually Reading the Outmost Eddies. I went with Exceptional Luck because it was simpler.<br /> <br /> First Impression was also part of the original Sphinx Attainments, but I mostly kept it because of how it builds upon Know Nature and Mental Scan. You study someone to learn more about them, and then you use that to approach them later on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fourth Attainment: Truth Without Knowledge</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 4, Investigation 4<br /> <br /> When entering an unexpected situation, the Sphinx may activate this Attainment to gain the benefits of Fools Rush In (p. 136), including its first Reach effect. In addition, the Sphinx may always activate this Attainment to gain extra dice for extended rolls to solve a puzzle, navigate a maze, conduct research, or deal with similarly difficult problems. Reach is spent on instant activation, Advanced Duration, and the spell's first Reach effect.<br /> <br /> Optional: Mind 4<br /> <br /> The Sphinx may gain the effects of Universal Language (p. 162). Reach is spent on instant activation and Advanced Duration. </div> </div> </div>Universal Language was another of the Sphinx's original Attainments, it was significant enough to the Legacy's themes that I wanted to keep it. I just needed to find a Fate spell to go along with it.<br /> <br /> Fools Rush In is actually quite weak for an Attainment, but when you apply its first Reach effect to extended rolls appropriate to the Sphinxes (which Quantum Flux can't do), it becomes just good enough. Besides, it's thematically appropriate for a Legacy like the Sphinxes; you instantly read a situation and figure out how to deal with it, even if you knew nothing about it beforehand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fifth Attainment: Writing The Pattern</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 5, Investigation 5<br /> <br /> The Sphinx contemplates the world for one scene, after which she activates this Attainment to replicate the effects of the spell Miracle (p. 140). This Attainment's Reach is spent on Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> Optional: Mind 5<br /> <br /> The Sphinx may activate this Attainment in order to gain the benefits of Incognito Presence (p. 160), including its Reach effect. Reach is spent on instant activation, Advanced Duration, Advanced Potency to add +1 to Clash of Wills rolls, and the spell's Reach effect. </div> </div> </div>Chaos Mastery and Miracle where the only Fate spells that seemed thematically appropriate for the fifth Attainment. Chaos Mastery was too complicated, so I picked Miracle.<br /> <br /> Using Incognito Presence for the Sphinx's weird stealth effect is something I knew I wanted to do before I even got started. I thought I couldn't neatly pull it off because I couldn't find the reference to Advanced Potency buffing Clash of Wills rolls in the Spell Factors section, but then I found it in the Clash of Wills section.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Miracle allows you to manipulate the pattern, while Incognito Presence allows you to hide inside it.<br /> <br /> Overall, working with Fixed Reach instead of against it made things much, much easier. Moving spells to higher Attainments made it a lot easier to capture the Sphinxes' core themes. It's also much easier if you focus on the original Attainments' narrative functions and try for similar effects instead of looking for a 1:1 conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":54,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","user":"Tiresias","date":". 05-10-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T15:10:56-07:00","id":892809,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I'm working on the House of Ariadne and I have sort of hit a stumbling block. Input would be greatly appreciated.</span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>DOCTRINE</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Time 2, Resolve 3, and one of the following skills at 2 dots or higher: Investigation, Survival, Streetwise, Socialize</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiation: Prospective Metropolitans must demonstrate patience by exploring their city and discovering a piece of their city\u2019s secret history to share with their local House.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Theory: The House of Ariadne understands that a city\u2019s culture -- special points of pride or contempt, its modes of speaking and thinking and doing -- will outlast even its buildings. A city\u2019s subtle, deathless power shapes mortal lives. A city is a god. It does not rule the concrete, brick, glass and wiring or the traffic, the businesses and the beggars. The City-god <i>is</i> them, <i>everything</i>, at once. Metropolitans believe all the many destinies, resonances and interconnections of Fate actually do form a diffuse entity with which they can commune and attempt to understand. Their methods provide indirect but definite proof of the City-god\u2019s reality.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Atypical of Acanthus is the dour demeanor and great patience of the House of the Ariadne. It is one of their key defining traits and it is emphasized several times in their write-up in <i>Legacies: the Sublime</i>, so I thought it was important. In order to reflect that, I chose to make uncommon Resolve part of the prerequisite for joining the Legacy in addition to the Arcane and mundane knowledge.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>MAGIC</b></span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling Arcanum: Time</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras: a place or time of great import to the city or its history (+1) finding a lost item meaningful to a community in the city (+2); teaching about the city\u2019s culture and history (+1); using self-annotated maps of neighborhoods or blueprints of buildings relevant to the casting of the spell (+2); getting lost and navigating to a familiar area (+1); photos and souvenirs from the city relevant to the casting of the spell (+1)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations: A walk in the city to find something you never saw before; exploring the subway tunnels; watching a sunrise or sunset from a penthouse apartment; visiting a museum or other tourist attraction; attending a party with a \u201clist;\u201d serving food at a homeless shelter; sleeping on a park bench.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ATTAINMENTS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The House\u2019s geomancy requires mastery of divination, but instead of focusing on a small item like a crystal or a pack of cards, Metropolitans use the expanse of the city to divine the past, present and future. The mage who wishes to follow Ariadne\u2019s thread must study Time and Fate. Much of the Metropolitans\u2019 powers come from walking a self-made Knot in the city. After seeing Ariadne\u2019s thread, the mage must attune herself to the city. A member of the House of Ariadne can attune herself to any city she is in. She will spend at least six hours walking through the city, following Ariadne\u2019s thread. During this time, she gets to know the city as the city itself gets a feel for her. The House of Ariadne never takes the direct route.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The trickiest part here is deciding what could be a Yantra vs what could be an Oblation. For the House of Ariadne they are practically interchangeable. </span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>First: Urban Communion</b><br /> Prerequisites: Initiation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once attuned to the city, she is its mother, sister, daughter, all at once. The Metropolitan spends one scene in communion with her city by whatever means she deems appropriate: a morning jog; feeding the pigeons in the park; reading the morning news in a random coffee shop; tagging graffiti in an alley; people-watching from a bus stop bench. For one day, the mage finds it exceedingly easy to get anywhere she wants to go in her city. This attainment works similarly to the spell \u201cGreen Light / Red Light\u201d: doors open for the Metropolitan, taxis and elevators arrive in the knick of time, and she never catches a red light or construction detour, etc. Reach is used for Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Optional:</b> Fate 1</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the mage spends a scene wandering the city streets, taking in the sights and partaking of a slice of the city life, the City will \u201cspeak\u201d to her and give her guidance on how to accomplish her stated goal. This attainment works similarly to the Fate 1 spell \u201cSerendipity\u201d with +1 Reach.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ll admit that I\u2019m still wrapping my head around the way Reach is used and the way Duration works. This is my understanding: \u201cGreen Light / Red Light\u201d has a primary factor of Duration, meaning it normally lasts for turns. By adding +1 Reach the Duration moves to the Prolonged chart, beginning at One Scene. Since this Attainment requires no roll, it gets two successes (2 dots in Time = 2 successes), even if it suffers the -2 penalty for making it last One Day per the chart -- still 2 successes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Is that how it works? I really need help here.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As for the choice of the attainment, I am getting real Jack Hawksmoor vibe from the House of Ariadne (for more information on that character, read Warren Ellis\u2019 run on <i>Stormwatch</i>. In that vein, I figured it would only be natural for the Metropolitans to have a sort of symbiotic relationship with the city. A keeper\u2019s and guardians of the city, the Metropolitans are kept and guarded by the city in turn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ll have some more attainments for them once I understand Reach and Temporal Sympathy and Withstanding better. I\u2019m not sure how those things apply to Attainments, if at all, and the Eleventh Question write-up doesn\u2019t seem to help me.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T15:20:11-07:00","id":892818,"title":"","content":"After throwing together my Mentats Legacy I actually like the Reach restrictions as they are, it pushes you to look at what you really want the Legacy to be able to always just <i>do</i> and what really ought to just be something the Mage casts as normal.<br /> <br /> I also have a feeling that Advanced Duration on Primary Factor: Duration spells that target the caster are going to be the mechanically &quot;best&quot; options most of the time: they're undispellable near-permanent buffs that don't take up a spell control slot, that's pretty powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T23:36:21-07:00","id":893072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=892809#post892809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ll admit that I\u2019m still wrapping my head around the way Reach is used and the way Duration works. This is my understanding: \u201cGreen Light / Red Light\u201d has a primary factor of Duration, meaning it normally lasts for turns. By adding +1 Reach the Duration moves to the Prolonged chart, beginning at One Scene. Since this Attainment requires no roll, it gets two successes (2 dots in Time = 2 successes), even if it suffers the -2 penalty for making it last One Day per the chart -- still 2 successes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Is that how it works? I really need help here.</span></span><br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ll have some more attainments for them once I understand Reach and Temporal Sympathy and Withstanding better. I\u2019m not sure how those things apply to Attainments, if at all, and the Eleventh Question write-up doesn\u2019t seem to help me.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Whole Legacy Reach problem is talked in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885225-2e-errata-needed-problem-with-legacies-attainments-as-written\">this topic</a> extensively - and I think that Errata should fix it. Still, even if you do not agree with my opinion, this topic is very good read, pointing to Legacy mechanics as should be used in now version of rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T00:45:35-07:00","id":893104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=892809#post892809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ll admit that I\u2019m still wrapping my head around the way Reach is used and the way Duration works. This is my understanding: \u201cGreen Light / Red Light\u201d has a primary factor of Duration, meaning it normally lasts for turns. By adding +1 Reach the Duration moves to the Prolonged chart, beginning at One Scene. Since this Attainment requires no roll, it gets two successes (2 dots in Time = 2 successes), even if it suffers the -2 penalty for making it last One Day per the chart -- still 2 successes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Is that how it works? I really need help here.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, it's not, you're smooshing several things together.<br /> <br /> First, the total successes don't matter (except for Exceptional Successes). Only Potency, Duration, Scale, and Range matter. Legacy Attainments don't roll to activate, they just automatically do. I honestly don't know why the &quot;number of successes&quot; line is in the Attainments section.<br /> <br /> Let's say you have the following spell, 2 dots in Fate, and Gnosis 2:<br /> <br /> <b>Fate **</b><br /> <br /> <b>Green Light / Red Light<br /> Practice: </b>Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Empathy, Science, Subterfuge<br /> Make a light green or red for the duration.<br /> <br /> Normally it would have a base duration of 2 turns (for your two dots in Fate), and 1 in every other factor (Potency, Area, &amp;c). You would have a base dicepool of 4 (Fate dots + Gnosis) and 1 free Reach. If you wanted to increase the duration even more you could take -2 penalties to further increase the duration, or you could increase one of the other factors by one step for every -2. You can also use Reach to make the spell instant cast (rather than ritual time) or use the Advanced spell factors table for a particular factor (Potency, Duration, Number of Subjects, Size, Area of Effect, and making it Sensory instead of touch each require an individual Reach).<br /> <br /> But that's for a regular spell, what about an Attainment?<br /> <br /> Attainments have fixed characteristics. Let's say your Attainment is the second Attainment and it reproduces GL/RL with Reach spent on Advanced Duration and your Fate is still 2 dots. Your Attainment GL/RL (AGLRL) can only be cast as a ritual because the Reach wasn't assigned to making it Instant cast, so it'll take 1 scene (i.e. 1 hour) to cast; but it does have Advanced Duration! But unlike a normal spell the factors are automatically assigned: your Arcanum dots improve the Primary Spell Factor, and secondary factors are improved by Arcanum/2 (rounded down).<br /> <br /> So AGLRL with the user at Fate 2 would have a duration of One Day (Duration is the Primary Factor and is Advanced), Potency 2 (base of 1 + 2/2), and Scale 2 (again, base of 1 + 2/2).<br /> <br /> If you used AGLRL with Fate 3, then the duration would be One Week, but Potency and other factors would remain 2 (base of 1 + 3/2 rounded down). You also would not gain any additional Reach, because Reach is fixed to the Dot rating of the Attainment with regards to the Dot rating of the spell, <i>not</i> the Dot rating of the user.<br /> <br /> <br /> If instead you had a Forces/Time Legacy attainment based on Turn Momentum with the Time 1 conjunctional then the secondary factors (in this case Duration and the Scales) would be based on the lower of Time dots or Forces dots divided by 2, instead of on Forces.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [EDIT]I'm actually iffy on if each type of Scale is separate or Scale is one thing. So it might be one Reach for Scale -&gt; Advanced Scale and each step up on Scale steps up every type of scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-18-2016, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:02:36-07:00","id":893228,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2757\" data-vbnamecard=\"2757\">proindrakenzol</a> I understand what you're saying, it's just that what you said isn't really in the book. For example, it says this under <b>Automatic Activation</b>: <i>the Attainment automatically acquires primary spell factor ranks (in Potency or Duration) equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the Attainment\u2019s highest prerequisite Arcanum.</i> I understand that 100%. But where does it say that the the Duration of the Spell/Attainment moves up the chart based on the number of successes you have? It only takes into account dice penalties.<br /> <br /> <i>What are primary spell factor ranks?</i> That term is used in no other place in the book.<br /> <br /> Any ideas about how Attainment activation competes with Withstanding/Sympathies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","user":"Troy","date":". 05-18-2016, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:21:02-07:00","id":893470,"title":"","content":"**Comment by Dave (Developer) on page 7**<br /> <br /> [Fan 2ED] Legacy: Tremere Lich<br /> Path: Moros<br /> Order: The Tremere have their own Nameless Order<br /> <br /> The Tremere are an iconic Mage antagonist.<br /> I am elated to see them return for 2nd edition with all the temptation Reaping brings.<br /> Inuring spells make spells more flexible for stealing souls and make it less critical to make Attainments for it.<br /> The need to keep using up souls balances the attainments power.<br /> <br /> <br /> Legacy Attainments<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st Eternal Need<br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> <br /> Upon joining the Legacy the Mage stops aging.<br /> His soul also slowly decays.<br /> After a year the soul has decayed completely and the Mage becomes Soulless (P.318).<br /> If the Mage gains the Thrall Condition, he ages the years he has been in the Tremere Legacy instantly.<br /> This may be fatal if enough years have past.<br /> The mage must therefore replace his soul at least once a year.<br /> The Attainment gives no benefit beyond this.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2nd The Mirror of the Soul<br /> Prerequisites: Death 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> The Tremere's soul appears like a normal Awakened soul without a Legacy when examined,<br /> for example with the &quot;Soul Marks&quot; spell.<br /> This keeps suspicious Mages from discovering that the Tremere has been eating souls.<br /> Hiding the 4th and 5th Attainment in this manner provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> The Tremere's Soulstones do not gain this protection.<br /> Upon gaining this Attainment the Tremere's soul erodes faster, needing a replacement every 6 months.<br /> If the Tremere attaches an Awakened soul to himself it will take twice as long to erode.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3rd Stolen Power<br /> Prerequisites: Death 3, Occult 3<br /> <br /> If the Tremere attaches an Awakened soul to himself, he gains Dots in one of the Arcana the owner of this soul knew.<br /> The new Arcana cannot have more dots than the Tremere has dots in the Death Arcana.<br /> The new Arcana does not stack.<br /> When the Soul has decayed, the new Arcana is lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> 4th Vessel for the Soul<br /> Prerequisites: Death 4<br /> <br /> As the spell &quot;Soul Jar&quot; (P.129). Three Reach is spent on both Reach options listed in the spell.<br /> Attached Sleeper souls now decay at a Rate of 1 per month.<br /> Awakened souls take 6 months.<br /> Joining a Tremere House (P.238) May change this Attainment.<br /> <br /> <br /> 5th Tithe<br /> Prerequisites: Death 5<br /> <br /> As the spell &quot;Sever the Awakened Soul&quot; (Death 5) P.133<br /> Attached Sleeper souls are now consumed at a Rate of 1 per month.<br /> Awakened souls take 6 months.<br /> Joining a Tremere House (P.238) May change this Attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":".  WHW makes a good point. 05-19-2016, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:47:59-07:00","id":893497,"title":"","content":"That third dot @__@. Still, as written, it sounds like you add dots to your preexisting dots; so stealing a soul of Life 2 Mage while you also have 2 Life would give you 4 Life. I personally would switch it to not stacking with anything; flat higher of the two.<br /> <br /> I now have a very weird urge to play someone tricked into becoming Tremere and being DARK AND MYSTERIOUS TORMENTED PROTAGONSIT who hunts other Left Handed Mages to sustain themselves. Still, you need Death 5 for that, becaue otherwise you will not be able to steal Awakened Souls. Eh. Might need an Artifact or Imbued Item...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:45:28-07:00","id":893627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=893228#post893228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2757\" data-vbnamecard=\"2757\">proindrakenzol</a> I understand what you're saying, it's just that what you said isn't really in the book. For example, it says this under <b>Automatic Activation</b>: <i>the Attainment automatically acquires primary spell factor ranks (in Potency or Duration) equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the Attainment\u2019s highest prerequisite Arcanum.</i> I understand that 100%. But where does it say that the the Duration of the Spell/Attainment moves up the chart based on the number of successes you have? It only takes into account dice penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say anything about successes because, as I said, successes are irrelevant.<br /> <br /> For Attainments all non-primary factors (e.g. if Potency is primary then Duration and Area are non-primary) move up equal to the lowest prerequisite Arcanum divided by 2, rounded down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>What are primary spell factor ranks?</i> That term is used in no other place in the book. </div> </div> </div>The position on the appropriate chart. So Forces 4 primary factor Potency would be Potency 4. Forces 4 primary factor Duration would be 5 turns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any ideas about how Attainment activation competes with Withstanding/Sympathies? </div> </div> </div>Withstand/Sympathies check the Potency of a spell/attainment. If the Potency is greater than that of the Withstand rating then the spell takes full effect on the target, if it's equal or less then the spell occurs but nothing actually happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:14:39-07:00","id":893707,"title":"","content":"Successes can be relevant to attainments since at 5 dots every activation would count as an Exceptional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:20:00-07:00","id":893712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=893707#post893707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Successes can be relevant to attainments since at 5 dots every activation would count as an Exceptional.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't roll to activate them, though. I, personally, wouldn't hand out Exceptional Success benefits for activating an Attainment, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T18:25:48-07:00","id":893769,"title":"","content":"I would, you can only get one mundane and maybe one arcane Beat per scene, if that's where the player wants it to come from because they're a Master I don't really care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T20:05:05-07:00","id":893825,"title":"","content":"Do you really want them to auto ignore Withstand or auto-regenerate Mana, making Mana-management irrelevant to Masters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T23:21:22-07:00","id":893872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=893470#post893470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Fan 2ED] Legacy: Tremere Lich<br /> Path: Moros<br /> Order: The Tremere have their own Nameless Order</div> </div> </div> </div>I will not write about Attinments as I still do not agree with corebook. But as to Parentage section - Legacy is Moros one, but Tremere are Nameless Order makes that they <b>inflitrate </b>every normal Global Order, even if they are from other Paths. Remember that previous Houses Legacies were diffrent Paths than Moros - like Mastigos ones in <i>To the Strongest</i> <b>Dark Eras</b>. So I envision now there are Tremere of all Paths there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T00:17:43-07:00","id":893880,"title":"","content":"My current plan for the Tremere is that they aren't a Legacy; they're a set of alterations to how Gnosis and Soul Loss work for a Tremere, and Houses are their Legacy-equivalents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T01:27:16-07:00","id":893900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=893880#post893880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current plan for the Tremere is that they aren't a Legacy; they're a set of alterations to how Gnosis and Soul Loss work for a Tremere, and Houses are their Legacy-equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Tremere will <b>not be seen</b> under Mage Sight, contrary to other Legacies? Only when House is employed on particular mage, something like Legacy Nimbus will be seen on Tremere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T02:16:15-07:00","id":893913,"title":"","content":"Consider that under the 1e rules, Tremere were hidden from Mage Sight anyway - as per Left Hand Path, they return results to anything looking at their soul or aura from the soul they're currently feeding from, not their Hollow Gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T02:55:13-07:00","id":893925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=893825#post893825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you really want them to auto ignore Withstand or auto-regenerate Mana, making Mana-management irrelevant to Masters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attainments aren't spells, just actions, as such they'd only accrue mundane Beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T02:59:45-07:00","id":893926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=893880#post893880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current plan for the Tremere is that they aren't a Legacy; they're a set of alterations to how Gnosis and Soul Loss work for a Tremere, and Houses are their Legacy-equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was the thought process behind this? I feel like the Tremere were a big reason (not necessarily the only one) as to 2e's soul loss mechanics, Wisdom/spell inuring, and Legacy Attainments not calling for Wisdom checks were all designed and implemented.<br /> <br /> Is making the Tremere an 'alternate template' (lack of better term), akin to what Banishers and Mad could be as well, a solution to a difficult problem that came up despite the above designs? Or was it always the plan behind the above mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T03:09:45-07:00","id":893930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=893880#post893880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current plan for the Tremere is that they aren't a Legacy; they're a set of alterations to how Gnosis and Soul Loss work for a Tremere, and Houses are their Legacy-equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even better!<br /> Trying to fit everything the Tremere are into a Legacy is hard.<br /> Can You spoil us a bit more on what is to come? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:33:35-07:00","id":894282,"title":"","content":"Celestial Orrery Rough Draft<br /> <br /> Keep the Oblations, needs Yantras<br /> <br /> Attainments:<br /> <br /> 1)<br /> Time: Momentary Flux Reach spent for Instant activation<br /> Prime: Pierce Deception Reach spent on Instant activation<br /> <br /> 2)<br /> Time: Divination Reach spent on Instant activation and the Reach clause for more specific info.<br /> Prime: Made up Compelling (Or Ruling) effect to duplicate the 1e effect of a Hallow paying the mana cost of a spell equal to Potency (Though it can't exceed the amount of mana currently in the Hallow). Reach spent on Instant activation. <br /> <br /> 3)<br /> Time: Shield of Chronos Reach spent for Instant Activation and Advanced Duration<br /> Prime: Sacred Geometry Reach for Advanced and Indefinite Duration as well as the +1 Reach Clause<br /> <br /> 4)<br /> Time:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-19-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:29:39-07:00","id":894533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=893880#post893880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current plan for the Tremere is that they aren't a Legacy; they're a set of alterations to how Gnosis and Soul Loss work for a Tremere, and Houses are their Legacy-equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, any idea when that blog/pdf updating the tremere is going to be out. My interest rised by 253%. I did the math.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T06:20:20-07:00","id":894684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=894282#post894282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial Orrery Rough Draft<br /> <br /> Keep the Oblations, needs Yantras<br /> <br /> Attainments:<br /> <br /> 1)<br /> Time: Momentary Flux Reach spent for Instant activation<br /> Prime: Pierce Deception Reach spent on Instant activation<br /> <br /> 2)<br /> Time: Divination Reach spent on Instant activation and the Reach clause for more specific info.<br /> Prime: Made up Compelling (Or Ruling) effect to duplicate the 1e effect of a Hallow paying the mana cost of a spell equal to Potency (Though it can't exceed the amount of mana currently in the Hallow). Reach spent on Instant activation.<br /> <br /> 3)<br /> Time: Shield of Chronos Reach spent for Instant Activation and Advanced Duration<br /> Prime: Sacred Geometry Reach for Advanced and Indefinite Duration as well as the +1 Reach Clause<br /> <br /> 4)<br /> Time:</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. When I finished the House of Ariadne I was going to do the Stewards of the Celestial Orrery next. I'm glad you beat me to it!<br /> I like what's going on here and I have some thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras:</b> In addition to the normal Sympathetic Yantras, you also use a lot of special Place and Time Yantras as well; the date of the subject's birth/creation (+1); the exact time of the subject's birth/creation (+1); using a general astrological chart for the subject (+1); creating an astrological chart specific to the subject (+2); consulting the mage's orrery (+1)<br /> <br /> Like the House of Ariadne, the Yantras and Oblations seem very interchangeable to me for this Legacy.<br /> <br /> I was thinking that one of the Prime additions to the Attainment would be the Words of Truth spell that takes effect whenever the Steward is speaking about a future they have divined. I kind of thought that would be cool and also give the Legacy an air of authority. Is there any way to make the Shield of Chronos permanent/indefinite as it was in first edition?<br /> <br /> I really like the Pierce Deception as an Attainment. I was going to use that, too. My view of the Stewards of the Celestial Orrerry is that this Legacy is the direct counter to the Seers and the Exarchs, one side of the same coin. Their faith leads them to believe that they are in touch with the signs and portents directly from the Oracles, so it is their duty to combat the works of the Exarchs wherever they find them. Since the Seers are a House of Lies, Pierce Deception and Words of Truth seem like good fits for the Stewards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T06:40:10-07:00","id":894688,"title":"","content":"It's a Reach to hit Advanced Duration and another Reach to make it of Indefinite Duration with a spell so I ruled it works for legacy &quot;always on&quot; effects as well. So yes, Shield of Chronos could stay on always by removing the Reach spent for Instant activation. If I'd moved it to the 4th attainment it would have used the false timeline projection as well.<br /> <br /> Words of Truth was definitely going to get worked in there at some point. If I put it at Prime 3 it can be instant and inflict a Condition, but I'm kind of tempted to put it at 4 and spend a Reach for Advanced Scale so they can sway small crowds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-20-2016, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T07:32:25-07:00","id":894709,"title":"","content":"Celestial Orrery Rough Draft<br /> <br /> Keep the Oblations, needs Yantras<br /> <br /> Attainments:<br /> <br /> 1)<br /> Time: Momentary Flux Reach spent for Instant activation<br /> Prime: Pierce Deception Reach spent on Instant activation<br /> <br /> 2)<br /> Time: Divination Reach spent on Instant activation and the Reach clause for more specific info.<br /> Prime: Made up Compelling (Or Ruling) effect to duplicate the 1e effect of a Hallow paying the mana cost of a spell equal to Potency (Though it can't exceed the amount of mana currently in the Hallow). Reach spent on Instant activation. <br /> <br /> 3)<br /> Time: Constant Presence Reach spent for Advanced and Indefinite Duration.<br /> Prime: Sacred Geometry Reach for Advanced and Indefinite Duration as well as the +1 Reach Clause<br /> <br /> 4)<br /> Time: Shield of Chronos: Reach spent for Advanced and Indefinite Duration and to activate the Reach Clause.<br /> Prime: Words of Truth. Reach spent for Instant Activation, Advanced Scale and the Reach Clause of the spell.<br /> <br /> 5) <br /> Time: Prophecy: One Reach spent for Instant Activation and another for the Reach clause.<br /> Prime: Screw it, going big, this mimics the effects of Geomancy with Reach spent on Advanced and Indefinite Duration and all left over Reach being spent on an effect to convert a Node into a Hallow with dots equal to Potency (2 if I understand secondary factors correctly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-20-2016, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:05:16-07:00","id":894752,"title":"","content":"I think that when it comes to your Indefinite Duration Attainments you can easily not spend that additional Reach.<br /> <br /> With Reach assigned to Advanced Duration, Prime 2 keeps that spell up for an entire day. With Prime 4, each of these spells lasts a week, with only a scene's worth of casting. At this point Reach spent on Indefinite Duration seems a waste. More than that: If the Attainment affects the Mage only, it will never be resisted. With a constant number of successes it will never fail. I think you can easily just make it constantly on. Legacy rules do allow some fudging.<br /> <br /> I you want to stay faithful to the Spellcasting mechanics, then Indefinite Duration Attainments are actually impossible, because you would have needed to take -10 in Spell Factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:23:46-07:00","id":894761,"title":"","content":"They are contested by anyone who wants to affect them by time traveling, figuring out what they're about to do, or revert what they've changed. Making it Indefinite removes the need to worry about upkeep, which yes isn't a huge concern to some. Allowing for Indefinite without a -10 penalty is how I've chosen to fudge the legacy. It's a valid use of Reach which I didn't otherwise have since those effects barely have anything to spend Reach on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:45:45-07:00","id":894773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=894761#post894761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are contested by anyone who wants to affect them by time traveling, figuring out what they're about to do, or revert what they've changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was that the Attainment won't be Withstood. The Spell succeeds and the protection is reliably on, even if other Mages manage to overcome it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=894761#post894761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making it Indefinite removes the need to worry about upkeep, which yes isn't a huge concern to some.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is my point. See below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=894761#post894761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allowing for Indefinite without a -10 penalty is how I've chosen to fudge the legacy. It's a valid use of Reach which I didn't otherwise have since those effects barely have anything to spend Reach on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you should get an Indefinite Duration without spending Reach for it. If you do spend it, you turn your back on a power you're allowed to have. If you don't, you can shift these Attainments down a slot and boost the others. If there is nothing to spend Reach on then it's definitely a problem. Still, it can be overcome with adding additional effects to enhance these Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:52:23-07:00","id":894775,"title":"","content":"I'm open to suggestions. That would be more helpful than just criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:45:33-07:00","id":894815,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Creative Thaumaturgy: A Time effect modeled after &quot;Web-Weaver&quot; (Space OOO) to enhance Temporal Sympathy. The original Stewards had it.<br /> <br /> Creative Thaumaturgy: A Time effect modeled after &quot;Shifting Sands&quot; (Time OOO) +1 Reach for Instant casting, +1 Reach for Sensory Range, +1 Reach for rewinding a Scene<br /> A tragedy turns out to have been a warning from an upcoming future. Legate's companions may receive them as well. In a way, it's a Spell invoked by the Player as opposed to the Character.<br /> <br /> &quot;Choose the Thread&quot; (Time OO) +1 Reach for Instant casting, +1 Reach for Sensory Range, +2 Reach for re-rolling supernatural powers<br /> Seems to be an appropriate spell. The Legate invokes a higher power keep the timeline on the right track.<br /> <br /> &quot;Temporal Summoning&quot; (Time OOO) +1 Reach for Instant casting, +1 Reach for Sensory Range, +1 Reach for Advanced Duration, +X Reach to give the target a Condition - Summoned people are Inspired to do the right thing, summoned objects have an improved Equipment Bonus. May summon targets from a possible future to serve as warning or encouragement.<br /> Sometimes a warrior grows infirm before their fated battle, a witness is murdered before trial or priceless knowledge is destroyed. This Spell brings them back. Not for good, but for long enough.<br /> <br /> Since Stewards stem from the Obrimos Path, extra Reach can be spent on inflicting beneficial Conditions, such as: Charmed, Guilty, Humbled, Inspired or Steadfast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 05-20-2016, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:51:53-07:00","id":894863,"title":"","content":"I did consider Choose the Thread, but it'd have to be the final attainment and I figured Prophecy was more in line with what they do.<br /> <br /> A new effect to strengthen Temporal Sympathy makes sense, though I'm not sure where I'd slot it in. Maybe as the 3rd attainment and then combine the current 3rd with the 4th? I'll have to look at Web Weaver.<br /> <br /> The rest, eh, I did consider those pretty intently especially Shifting Sands but ultimately decided that Augurs seem to be motivated to move forward through Time as long as its towards the future they envision, and they don't seem very intent on do-overs. Hence the Time shield and veil to keep others from messing with their vision of the future by editing their past or maneuvering them by knowing what they've done/will do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:05:25-07:00","id":894870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=894863#post894863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A new effect to strengthen Temporal Sympathy makes sense, though I'm not sure where I'd slot it in. Maybe as the 3rd attainment and then combine the current 3rd with the 4th? I'll have to look at Web Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>The third slot seems like the right place. As for the rest - it looks like you know what you're doing. If you're willing to &quot;cheat&quot; you can create a Prime effect that Contests all Time Spells that would interfere with the Steward. That would free a few slots among the Time Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:30:57-07:00","id":894892,"title":"","content":"One thing I have been kicking around and considering implementing in my conversions is that if the power has a significant limitation in its flexibility, or a drawback that is associated with its use of always being on, it acts in place of a reach requirement.<br /> <br /> <b>1) Limitations of the attainment are significant compared to the base spell. </b>For example, Tamers of Fire. Their forces attainments only influence fire, despite the practices their attainments are based on usually would allow them to manipulate all elements. Thus, I would grant them finer control with that attainment in exchange for the loss of reach, and grant 1 more reach for determining reach for that spell (so they can instantly rule fire at sensory range as rank 2 attainment, for example.) <br /> <br /> <b>2) Drawbacks are inherent and actually limiting, especially if the mage can't remove them.</b> For example would be making a strong life or mind shield permanent, but having it that the mage must apply the effects against all spells that are not his own, including beneficial ones. Or things like the Tremere, who have a pretty big drawback (though Dave has mentioned they essentially with have a new template, so maybe not as applicable). So while making the effect indefinite normally would eat 2 reach, it eats one as the drawbacks &quot;pay&quot; for one of those Reach.<br /> <br /> <b>3) Reach benefit is situational and doesn't always provide a bonus, or the effects they create are situational and don't provide a benefit that outweighs a temporary one significantly.</b>Another aspect is if the indefinite has as much of a drawback as having to restore the effect once in a while. Take moving ley lines. Permanently shifting them could lead to as many complications as allowing them to lapse, as resonances may change or the location may no longer be as friendly to the mage as it had when the lines were first moved. The fact that having them permantly that way do to attainment use means the mage would have to work to undo what he created, and others could exploit the creations without having to invest any effort. On the other hand, having to maintain the lines adds a time commitment to the mage, but also means they can let them lapse and not let a rival seize their work unless their rival invest maintaining it, and any mistakes made can be allowed to lapse on their own. When this scenario occurs, I would consider offering the flexibility.<br /> <br /> Now, I am asking for feedback on these ideas; these are thoughts I have had to balance both recreating the 1e Legacies while also keeping them balanced. I ranked them by the strength of my comfort with such implementation (I.e. I feel that #1 is most easily justified, while 3 is more tricky) and I wasn't extensive (under #1 I would consider the effects of the concentration Yantra a fair limit, but didn't want to flesh out the mechanical implementation here yet). But any feedback would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-20-2016, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:49:12-07:00","id":894916,"title":"","content":"I feel like that makes sense, attainments that are a limited version of a spell are supposed to remain of a roughly equal quality to the broader spell its modeled on.<br /> <br /> Though the ley line shifting one I threw up there I figured, hey, they can always put it back. Unless they're Jonathan Strange and just somehow never find the time to get around to it.<br /> <br /> Looking over the 11Q I totally forgot to spend Reach for sensory range so I'm going to have to do some revision for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:55:14-07:00","id":894919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=894892#post894892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>1) Limitations of the attainment are significant compared to the base spell. </b>For example, Tamers of Fire. Their forces attainments only influence fire, despite the practices their attainments are based on usually would allow them to manipulate all elements. Thus, I would grant them finer control with that attainment in exchange for the loss of reach, and grant 1 more reach for determining reach for that spell (so they can instantly rule fire at sensory range as rank 2 attainment, for example.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done this when updating my Legacy. The Spell &quot;Correspondence&quot; can detect Sympathetic Connections of a particular type for +2 Reach. When designing an Attainment I narrowed it's scope to the point it would normally require that Reach, but I made it unable to find Connections of any other type. That's why I ignored that additional cost. It's not an exact science. I feel that Reach spent on Spell Factors is usually more potent than Reach spent on additional effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=894892#post894892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>2) Drawbacks are inherent and actually limiting, especially if the mage can't remove them.</b> For example would be making a strong life or mind shield permanent, but having it that the mage must apply the effects against all spells that are not his own, including beneficial ones. Or things like the Tremere, who have a pretty big drawback (though Dave has mentioned they essentially with have a new template, so maybe not as applicable). So while making the effect indefinite normally would eat 2 reach, it eats one as the drawbacks &quot;pay&quot; for one of those Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shielding Spells can be cast on others without spending Reach, as long as you touch the target. If such Attainment only affects the Legate, I consider it limiting enough to enhance the Spell in a different way. If the Attainment uses it's Reach on Instant Casting, it can be refreshed every few turns with no risk of failure. If it uses it's Reach on Advanced Duration, it takes longer to cast but doesn't need refreshing that often. At this point I feel the Attainment can as well be always on. More than that, I feel it should be possible to activate and deactivate with a turn's concentration.<br /> <br /> One more thing I did was to give a few Attainment an honest to God extra point of Reach. To balance it I decided the Mage needs to constantly focus to uphold the Spell, otherwise it ends. I'm not sure if it's sufficiently balanced, but I do hope so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:57:37-07:00","id":894921,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2813_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2813\" data-vbnamecard=\"2813\">Freemind</a>, sorry, but I think that you should be in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885225-2e-errata-needed-problem-with-legacies-attainments-as-written\">this topic</a> - it's exactly on thread subject. Other than this - yeah, I can agree with those ideas for higher Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:00:12-07:00","id":894927,"title":"","content":"Since I'm here, I'd like to repost my update where it will be visible.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885637-2e-homebrew-fangs-of-mara#post885637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fangs of Mara</b><br /> Nickname: Nightmares<br /> <br /> Parentage: Mastigos (However, in such a small Legacy tutors rarely discriminate based on the Path) Nameless, Seers of the Throne, Guardians of the Veil<br /> Background: Legacies, the Sublime, page 139<br /> Appearance: Legacies, the Sublime, page 138<br /> <br /> Ruling Arcanum: Mind<br /> Yantras: Succeeding on an Empathy or Intimidation roll relevant to the spell (+2), Withstanding or inflicting torture (+2), Any records of nightmares and trauma (+1, +2 if tailored to the spell), Comfort objects (+1, +2 if tailored to the spell)<br /> Oblations: Studying or recording relevant Lore, Inflicting nightmares or trauma, Leading a successful therapy session, Brainwashing or deprogramming, In-depth psychoanalysis, Facing or indulging one's fears<br /> <br /> <b>Attainment 1</b><br /> Prerequisites: Mind 2. Empathy 2 or Intimidate 2. Must have entered dreams of an Intruder<br /> <br /> &quot;Soul Diagnostics&quot; (Mind 1) modeled after Soul Marks (Death 1)<br /> This Attainment works like the spell it's based on, except it utilizes the Mind Arcanum. Fangs use this power to detect the tell-tale marks of Acamoth influence. The Attainment can even be used to recognize Intruders on sight, but it's notoriously unreliable in this capacity. 1 Reach assigned to Instant casting.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: Space 1</b><br /> <br /> Correspondence (Space 1)<br /> Fangs of Mara always focus on what others don't want to confront. They can easily read Sympathetic Links to sources of trauma, anxiety and self-destructive behaviors. While it doesn't give them insight into the nature of these traumas, it gives them a springboard for investigation. The Wiser Fangs occasionally use this Attainment on themselves, to resolve their personal issues. 1 Reach assigned to Instant casting. Searching for specific Sympathetic Links usually demands +2 Reach. However, in case of this Attainment this cost is waived, since the Attainment is of limited use compared to the original Spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainment 2</b><br /> Prerequisites: Mind 2. Empathy 3 or Intimidate 3<br /> <br /> &quot;Fear's Icy Hand&quot; (Mind 2) modeled after Exceptional Luck (Fate 2)<br /> Fangs know first-hand how erroneous thought patterns and unregulated emotions can lead to failure of the worst kind. While their standards demand that they shouldn't freely inflict what they can't take. By this point of their development, they can take a lot. This Attainment imposes a dice penalty equal to Potency to all mundane actions the subject takes for as long as the Fang can focus on casting. 1 Reach assigned to Instant casting. An extra Reach is assigned to Sensory Range, so to balance the effect, it's Duration drops to length of concentration.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: Space 2</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Nondetection&quot; (Mind 2) modeled after Supernal Veil (Prime 2)<br /> Fangs make enemies easily. When spying on Intruders, Scelesti or more respectable Mages, it is better not to make ones presence known. This Attainment works like the Spell it's based on, but it only covers Legacy Attainments and Mind Spells cast by the user. 1 Reach assigned to Instant casting. Since the Attainment is so easy to cast, it can effectively be always active. The Fang can turn it on and off with a turn of concentration.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainment 3</b><br /> Prerequisites: Mind 3. Empathy 3 or Intimidate 3. The other Skill at 2 or one of the following at 2 (Investigate, Medicine, Occult, Stealth, Subterfuge)<br /> <br /> Befuddle (Mind 3)<br /> By studying imperfections of the mind, Fangs can reach the underlying framework beneath thoughts and feelings and interfere with what they find there. 1 Reach assigned to Instant casting. An extra Reach is assigned to Sensory Range, so to balance the effect, it's Duration drops to length of concentration.<br /> <br /> <b>OR</b><br /> <br /> Augment Mind (Mind 3)<br /> The Fang carries the trauma of their initiation like a badge of honor. Or a shield. The knowledge of what they survived gives them the strength to continue on whatever path they choose. When this Attainment is developed, the Fang chooses to increase a single Attribute, which can't ever be changed. The Fang can boost this Attribute beyond their Gnosis maximum. This Attainment is mostly used to enhance Resolve or Composure, but Presence is not unknown. 1 Reach assigned to Instant Casting. The spell can't be used on others. Since the Attainment is so easy to cast, it can effectively be always active. The Fang can turn it on and off with a turn of concentration.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: Space 3</b><br /> <br /> Web-Weaver (Space 3)<br /> Dark portions of the Astral? Dreams of Intruders? A strange Emanation Realm? Everyone is bound by fear and whatever the medium, Fangs learn to tap into it. When using Legacy Attainments and Mind Spells through Sympathetic Casting, the Fang treats their Sympathetic Connection to the target as one step stronger for every point of Potency. This can step up a non-existent connection and bring the Sympathetic Withstand down to zero. The connection is strictly one way - it does not make the user any more vulnerable to retaliation. 1 Reach assigned to Instant casting. Since the Attainment is so easy to cast, it can effectively be always active. The Fang can turn it on and off with a turn of concentration.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Attainment 4</b><br /> Prerequisites: Mind 4, Empathy 4 or Intimidate 4<br /> <br /> Hallucination/Terrorize (Mind 4)<br /> This Spell resembles Hallucination, except it can only evoke nightmarish visions. The Fang may choose to tailor them to the target, or to let target's subconscious and perhaps other factors to create their content. As long as the Spell is in effect the Fang can inflict the Insensate Tilt on their victim or let the Game Master choose an appropriate Tilt. This Attainment can be used for communication, but all transmissions become strongly disturbing. Fangs regularly use it for this purpose anyway. 1 Reach assigned to Instant casting. An extra Reach is assigned to Sensory Range, so to balance the effect, it's Duration drops to length of concentration.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: Space 4</b><br /> <br /> Dream Reaching (Mind 2)<br /> The Fang can enter a dream of a sleeping creature - Be it a Sleeper, Awakened, Intruder or something else besides. Even before initiation into the Legacy, this is the first spell prospective Fangs learn - one they will use multiple times until the end. The Spell can be cast Instantly when in contact with the target, or with a scene's meditation when not. Either way the effect lasts a scene, unless repeated. Curiously, this Attainment gives Fangs a recognizable tell when in the Astral. Their Silver Thread turns into a heavy chain. Some Legates are still studying the ramifications. 1 Reach remains to be spent upon use either on Sensory Range or Instant Casting. 2 Reach are assigned to an additional effect - the Fang can shift between observing the dream and being an active part of it with a turn of concentration.<br /> <br /> <i>Notably, entering the dreams of Intruders is not entirely reliable. Gulmoth that approximate physical creatures dream reasonably often, but the anatomy of their dreams can &quot;surprise&quot; even an experienced Fang. Sometimes, investigators can't step back from being participators in the dreams. In some cases, suffering Soul-Shock is a lethal proposition. In all cases delving deeper into the Oneiros is... advanced. Acamoth, being Goetia, don't dream except in very rare cases. The brave Fang who entered one such dream has been since kept sedated and comfortable. New Fangs are brought to him to hopefully learn something and then leave laughing nervously about &quot;Abyssception&quot;. Rare, strange Abyssal phenomena dream even though they don't approach being a discrete entity. Fangs have managed to quarantine an Abyssal Verge after discovering that the very narrative of entering it seemed to dream.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Attainment 5</b><br /> Prerequisites: Mind 5, Empathy 4 or Intimidate 4. The other Skill at 3 or one of the following at 3 (Investigate, Medicine, Occult, Stealth, Subterfuge)<br /> <br /> Psychic Reprogramming (Mind 4)<br /> For their studies, Fangs use this Attainment to alter their target's psyche and see if their susceptibility to Acamoth influence changes, but it has many other uses as well. Some Fangs use it for therapy or even alleviating the damage they left. The Attainment can be used either within Dreams through a scene-long ritual or Instantly through physical contact. In the last case, sitting on a sleeping target's chest is a Legacy's tradition. 1 Reach Assigned to Advanced Duration. 1 Reach remains to be spent upon use either on Sensory Range or Instant Casting.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: Space 5</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Back Door&quot; (Space 4) modeled after Supernal Dispellation (Prime 4)<br /> Fangs take the lessons of their Third Attainment and take them to their logical end. This Attainment works like the spell it's based on, but only as an aide for using Legacy Attainments and Mind Spells and only to suppress Wards and similar protections than stand in their way. 1 Reach assigned to Instant casting. 1 Reach assigned to Sensory Range. Since the Attainment is so easy to cast, it can effectively be always active. The Fang can turn it on and off with a turn of concentration.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885637-2e-homebrew-fangs-of-mara?p=887171#post887171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fangs of Mara and the Astral<br /> <br /> Fangs have all the means and reasons to maintain a stronghold in their Temenotic realm. Considering their need for secrecy and how easily each individual's experiences can be lost, Fangs regularly network and review their results. Unfortunately, either due to their actions, or their usual thoughts, the area was frequently a target of Acamoth interest. Fangs have made lemonade out of lemons and took the opportunity to study the Enemy on their conditions. The realm had to be erased a few times to prevent corruption, and each time &quot;non-vital&quot; knowledge was lost. It's one of the reasons Fangs often squirrel away records in the Material Realm. Now, with proper Security in place, most Acamoth are either unaware of the place or are captured and quarantined. The more worrying are the ones that deliberately stay away. Even those that don't intend a confrontation can sell their knowledge to someone who does.<br /> <br /> In the depths of the Astral, off the road between Temenos and Anima Mundi there is a realm containing the rawest of human nightmares. It has always been of interest to Fangs of Mara, but between their numbers and the challenges of studying the place they still feel woefully ignorant. Even then they count among their number the foremost experts on the region. Their research allowed them to discover an important phenomenon - intense experiences, especially those caused by the supernatural, leave a temporary Imprint in the realm. Patrolling the realm allows to discover sites of recent supernatural activity, including places where Sleepers were damaged by Dissonance. Fangs can use this phenomenon to search for Scelesti and Intruders, but those who do usually become quite informed about other Things that bump in the night. Some Fangs use the information to earn goodwill with the local Orders - a way of keeping oneself useful. However, there exists a factor that discourages careless entry. Aside from the usual dangers of the Astral, Fangs occasionally become targets of scrutiny by a powerful presence. What happens next varies. Travelers have found themselves taken to an important Imprint - possibly of their own making, confronted with their fears and desires, trapped with a monstrous Goetia, or even back in the Material Realm, far off from where they meditated. Of those who survive the ordeal, most reports have one thing in common - a sense of deranged love Fangs feel directed towards them. It's an unnerving experience and as far as Fangs know, there are no records of other Mages going through it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:03:24-07:00","id":894930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=894921#post894921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2813_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2813\" data-vbnamecard=\"2813\">Freemind</a>, sorry, but I think that you should be in <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885225-2e-errata-needed-problem-with-legacies-attainments-as-written&quot;]this</a> topic[/URL] - it's exactly on thread subject. Other than this - yeah, I can agree with those ideas for higher Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure he's discussing good methods for updating legacies to 2e, not complaining about a lack of Reach like you. So he's on point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:15:48-07:00","id":894939,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> That bit about the Astral and the Fangs is pretty damn cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:44:46-07:00","id":894963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=894930#post894930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure he's discussing good methods for updating legacies to 2e, not complaining about a lack of Reach like you. So he's on point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is also part of discussing Reach mechanics. I would not complain on seeing mechanics of Reach in 2E if options like this would be posted in corebook than bland &quot;only 1 free Reach&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T14:04:40-07:00","id":894978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=894963#post894963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is also part of discussing Reach mechanics. I would not complain on seeing mechanics of Reach in 2E if options like this would be posted in corebook than bland &quot;only 1 free Reach&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>They sorta are implied, when it says you can break the rules and adjust attainments as needed. I am just looking for feedback as you possible ways to do so, not have said changes added to the book. Hence why I posted here. <br /> <br /> Though if it seems more appropriate, I can also start a new discussion thread (since I don't feel it fits in the errata thread either as previously mentioned.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T14:05:25-07:00","id":894980,"title":"","content":"The rules do also say to bend rules for attainments to make them the equivalent of a more broadly applicable spell when they govern a more specific instance of what that spell might cover.<br /> <br /> Also, your thread is literally entitled Problems with legacy attainments and Freemind doesn't have a problem. This thread is asking for ideas for updating legacies to 2e, and that's what Freemind is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T11:16:09-07:00","id":895581,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Daoine</b></div> <br /> I took a crack at the Daoine while I was born. Once again, I can't shake the feeling that it would be much easier to just build a new Legacy from the ground up than trying to convert an existing one, but to hell with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>First Attainment: Black Cat's Passing</b><br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> <br /> The Good Folk know the best way to punish the sins of the guilty. This attainment mimics the effects of &quot;Serendipity&quot; (p. 135), save that the Mage can only use it when she wishes to learn the most effective way to punish or hurt someone. Reach is spent on instant activation.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Time 1<br /> <br /> The Daoine spends one scene contemplating an omen she received using the first attainment. She may then ask specific questions about how her omen can come to pass, per &quot;Divination&quot; (p. 186) and its Reach effect. </div> </div> </div>Why Time instead of Mind? For one thing, using a non-ruling Arcanum for optional effects is kind of a dick move. For another, I don't think the Daoine used Mind very well in the first place. Plus, I thought of a really cool thing you can do with Time 5. <br /> <br /> Attainment-wise, Serendipity is a nice little effect that has some good synergy with Divination. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Second Attainment: The Faerie Mask</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 2, Occult 2<br /> <br /> The Daoine spends a scene in seclusion and masks her destiny, allowing her to evade the curses of others. This attainment functions as &quot;Fabricate Fortune&quot; (p. 136). Reach is spent on advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Time 2<br /> <br /> By reading the weave of Time, the Daoine may distinguish saints from sinners. This attainment functions as &quot;Momentary Flux&quot; (p. 187). Reach is spent on instant activation and sensory range. </div> </div> </div>This one's mostly a filler, since I couldn't find any Fate or Time effects that worked here. I do like Momentary Flux though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Third Attainment: The Evil Eye</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 3, Occult 3<br /> <br /> The Mage touches her victim and places a terrifying curse upon her. This attainment functions per &quot;Exceptional Luck&quot; (p. 135), save that it can only be used to place hexes on someone. Reach is spent on instant activation and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Time 3<br /> <br /> The Daoine may supplement any use of the third attainment with the effect of &quot;Hung Spell&quot; (p. 188). The effect of the hex only takes place when Hung Spell's duration expires, when the Mages chooses to relinquish the Hung Spell effect, or when some conditions set by the Fate 2 attainment Conditional Duration are met. Regardless, using this optional attainment always costs one point of mana. Reach is spent on instant activation and advanced duration. </div> </div> </div>This one is the bread and butter attainment. The name doesn't really work, but I do like the idea of touch-based curses. It's unsettling, and it leads to the last attainment nicely enough. Hung Spell has very good synergy here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fourth Attainment: The Eternal Wheel</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 4, Occult 4<br /> <br /> The Daoine spends one scene meditating upon the skein of destiny, after which she gains the benefits of &quot;Interconnections&quot; (p. 134). Reach is spent on Interconnections' additional Reach effects, as well as advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: Time 4</b><br /> <br /> While the main effect of the fourth attainment is active, the Daoine may spend a point of mana in order to study a specific subject under &quot;Postcognition&quot; (p. 187). This can allow the Mage to see how a subject's destiny has changed over time. Reach is spent on instant activation, sensory activation, advanced duration, and the reach effect to &quot;scrub&quot; the visions. </div> </div> </div>Not much to say here. Interconnections and Postcognition are both staple powers, and they work fairly well together. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fifth Attainment: Doom of Promise</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 5, Occult 5<br /> <br /> The Daoine confirms an oath with a touch or handshake, sealing it with &quot;Oaths Fulfilled&quot; (p. 135). Reach is spent on instant activation, advanced duration, and all of the spell's optional Reach effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Time 5<br /> <br /> The Good Folk have no need for first chances. Whenever someone breaks an oath made with the fifth attainment's standard, the Daoine may spend one scene in meditation and spend one point of mana in order to return to the moment the oath was sanctified per &quot;Corridors of Time&quot; (p. 191). Once there, the Mage <i>must</i> curse the oathbreaker using the Legacy's third attainment, after which she returns to the present. Reach is spent on sensory activation in order to make use of Temporal Sympathy. </div> </div> </div>This one's my favourite. Oaths Fulfilled is a direct conversion from first edition Daoine, and pairing it with Corridors of Time lets you go back in time and retroactively curse people who have betrayed your trust. I love it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T16:46:03-07:00","id":895744,"title":"","content":"The problem going with Fate and Time is that you basically screw over Acanthus by giving them a double ruling arcana with the weak XP rebate, and screw over other Paths by making them buy up an extra common arcana to benefit from the Optional arcana. I agree that the Mind part of the Daoine wasn't that great, but it could have certainly been reworked, or you could have gone with a different arcana setup altogether that would fit.<br /> <br /> I'm also kind of surprised that you didn't include the ability from Fate 1 to know when a target has transgressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T16:48:26-07:00","id":895746,"title":"","content":"You don't get screwed by buying Common Arcana, it costs the same amount of XP. It's just different type of XP past 3rd dot, which is hardly problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T17:36:19-07:00","id":895766,"title":"","content":"Good point, I forgot they didn't make Ruling arcana cheaper. Still not great though since as I said they have to invest in a 4th arcana (Smart but not necessarily desirable) to be able to unlock the Optional arcana attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T18:45:31-07:00","id":895805,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the Celestial Orrery writeups I think whoever said Shifting Sands isn't appropriate as an attachment is correct. They are diviners not types that are trying solutions for a possible present. They are more about long term possible future, prophecy and destiny. Especially their favored version of it. Similar to a Bene Gesserit in many ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T19:06:17-07:00","id":895812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=895581#post895581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one is the bread and butter attainment. The name doesn't really work, but I do like the idea of touch-based curses. It's unsettling, and it leads to the last attainment nicely enough. Hung Spell has very good synergy here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate's Grasp, Touch of Doom, Mark of Burden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T19:29:18-07:00","id":895832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=895805#post895805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for all the Celestial Orrery writeups I think whoever said Shifting Sands isn't appropriate as an attachment is correct. They are diviners not types that are trying solutions for a possible present. They are more about long term possible future, prophecy and destiny. Especially their favored version of it. Similar to a Bene Gesserit in many ways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mind you the Reach has to be respent to move the attainments that look through Time to Sensory Range in order to use Temporal Sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T15:27:53-07:00","id":896338,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is the <b>House of Ariadne's</b> attainments all worked out into one cohesive rough draft.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For more information on this Legacy, see <i>Legacies: The Sublime</i>, p 53 - 61</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">DOCTRINE</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Time 2, Resolve 3, and one of the following skills at 2 dots or higher: Investigation, Stealth, Survival, Streetwise, Socialize, Subterfuge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiation: Prospective Metropolitans must demonstrate patience by exploring their city and discovering a piece of their city\u2019s secret history to share with their local House.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Organization: Each city has one House, regardless of the city\u2019s size. Each House is divided into the Trackers and the Weavers. The Weavers are the elder, experienced members of the Legacy and, while they train the Trackers, they plan the City\u2019s future and manage its secrets according to the City\u2019s will. The Trackers spend their time finding lost people and items, uncovering the secrets and the history of their City.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Theory: The House of Ariadne understands that a city\u2019s culture -- special points of pride or contempt, its modes of speaking and thinking and doing -- will outlast even its buildings. A city\u2019s subtle, deathless power shapes mortal lives. A city is a god. It does not rule the concrete, brick, glass and wiring or the traffic, the businesses and the beggars. The City-god <i>is</i> them, <i>everything</i>, at once. Metropolitans believe all the many destinies, resonances and interconnections of Fate actually do form a diffuse entity with which they can commune and attempt to understand. Their methods provide indirect but definite proof of the City-god\u2019s reality.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">MAGIC</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling Arcanum: Time</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras: a place or time of great import to the city or its history (+1) finding a lost item meaningful to a community in the city (+2); teaching about the city\u2019s culture and history (+1); using self-annotated maps of neighborhoods or blueprints of buildings relevant to the casting of the spell (+2); getting lost and navigating to a familiar area (+1); photos and souvenirs from the city relevant to the casting of the spell (+1)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations: A walk in the city to find something you never saw before; exploring the subway tunnels; watching a sunrise or sunset from a penthouse apartment; visiting a museum or other tourist attraction; attending a party with a \u201clist;\u201d serving food at a homeless shelter; sleeping on a park bench.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>First Attainment: Urban Communion</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once attuned to the city, she is its mother, sister, daughter, all at once. The Metropolitan spends one scene in communion with her city by whatever means she deems appropriate: a morning jog; feeding the pigeons in the park; reading the morning news in a random coffee shop; tagging graffiti in an alley; people-watching from a bus stop bench. For one day, the mage finds it exceedingly easy to get anywhere she wants to go in her city. This attainment works similarly to the spell \u201cGreen Light / Red Light\u201d: doors open for the Metropolitan, taxis and elevators arrive in the knick of time, and she never catches a red light or construction detour, etc. Reach is used for Advanced Duration.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Optional Arcanum: Fate 1</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the mage spends a scene wandering the city streets, taking in the sights and partaking of a slice of the city life, the City will \u201cspeak\u201d to her and give her guidance on how to accomplish her stated goal. This attainment works similarly to the Fate 1 spell \u201cSerendipity\u201d with +1 Reach.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>This one is pretty straightforward. Metropolitans have a communion with their city that makes it easier for them to get around and mingle with folks. The city is her constant companion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Second Attainment: Stir of Echoes</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Time 2, Investigation 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once the mage has reached communion with her city, she can use the Stir of Echoes attainment in order to get a feel for the city\u2019s history. This resembles the Time 1 spell \u201cPostcognition,\u201d with Potency equal to the mage\u2019s Time dots. The Metropolitan spends a scene wandering the city as she follows Ariadne\u2019s thread and the city begins to speak to her, relating its past to the mage. While the mage might not know names, she can tell if and when a man was murdered on this street corner, or if a couple made love in a park or if a mage committed a vulgar spell in a movie theater. The symbolism of the city makes itself known to the mage as the city\u2019s resonance applies meanings to different things. +1 Reach is assigned to Advanced Duration; +1 Reach is assigned to Sensory Range for Temporal Sympathy. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Optional Arcanum: Fate 2</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can also get a sense of the destinies of people, places, and objects that she observes in her city and in its history. The attainment duplicates the effects of the Fate 1 spell \u201cInterconnections\u201d with a Potency equal to the mage\u2019s Fate dots. +1 Reach is assigned to Advanced Scale; +1 Reach is assigned to detect alterations to destinies, including possession and supernatural mind control. </span></span> </div> </div> </div><b>EDIT</b>: Altered the Reach Assignment to account for Temporal Sympathy/Sensory Range. This is the reconstruction of the First Edition Attainment. I'm still unsure how a fixed Potency attainment can overcome the Withstanding necessary for Temporal Sympathy. I guess it's just a matter of more power/knowledgeable mages having the ability to look back further in time. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Third Attainment: Discovery Mediation</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Time 3, Fate 3, Investigation 3. Additionally, the Metropolitan must have at least two dots in two of the other possible skills required to learn this Legacy\u2019s attainments. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This power is the bailiwick of the Metropolitans. Given enough time (and patience) Ariadne\u2019s thread will always lead the mage to whatever she is looking for. The mage must focus her mind on what she is trying to find and spend at least one scene wandering her city to follow the Knot of Ariadne\u2019s thread. The mage can search for any item or person, general or specific. She is even capable of finding more abstract subjects like Hallows, spatial rifts, or a specific murder-spirit (though she doesn\u2019t have the means to observe or interact with them without the appropriate Arcana). As long as the subject is in her city, the mage doesn\u2019t need to have sympathetic connection to the subject. Ariadne\u2019s thread will lead her to where it is, but the path will not be direct. This process is actually an amalgamated and oblique use of Time 1s \u201cDivination\u201d and Fate 2s \u201cShifting the Odds\u201d with Potency equal to the mage\u2019s Time dots. Reach is assigned to Sensory Range.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Following the thread of Fate may take some time, and if the mage seeks a kidnapped colleague, the mage has no guarantee the person won\u2019t be dead when the mage finds her. The meditation will not work if the subject leaves the material plane; the trail simply goes cold. If the subject of the Discovery Mediation is kept behind considerable defenses, whether locked doors, vaults or magical protection, Ariadne\u2019s thread will not give the mage any abilities to bypass the security. The thread will surely lead the way to the desired subject, but does not tell you the best, or safest, way to get there.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>EDIT:</b> Assigned Reach to Sensory Range. This is the reconstruction of their First Edition 2nd Attainment. I think this works out pretty well without the need to assign Reach and stuff. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fourth Attainment: Into the Labyrinth</b><br /> Prerequisites: Time 4, Investigation 3, Streetwise 3. Additionally, the Metropolitan must have at least 3 dots in one other Doctrine skill or two dots in three of the possible Doctrine skills. </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In times of dire need, the Metropolitan can call upon her city to to protect her from adversaries. Ariadne\u2019s thread leads her to exactly the right place at the right time, while Fate itself conspires to keep her enemies at bay. Anyone foolish enough to follow her will find themselves in a place that has suddenly become a confusing maze filled with danger. The mage spends 1 mana and an instant action to activate this attainment, which confers the benefits of the Safe Place Merit equivalent to the mage\u2019s Time dots for one scene. As long as the mage stays in the same general location (inside an apartment building, wandering the same city block, in a crowded mall) she is afforded this protection.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a new effect inspired by the whole Ariadne myth. I know that the House of Ariadne stirs up trouble and I want to give them an attainment that works as a form of self-defense. Again, the idea is that the Metropolitan is in communion with her city and she is never alone. The city itself will rally to her defense when she needs it to. I wasn't entirely sure if this should be the Third or Fourth Attainment. I think both effects are pretty cool and powerful. I think I made it the Fourth Attainment just to break up the pattern of divination powers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fifth Attainment: Geomantic Meditation</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Time 5, Resolve 4, Investigation 4. Additionally, the Metropolitan must have 3 dots in three other Doctrine skills or two or more dots in all possible Doctrine skills.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this power, the House of Ariadne move from their role as discoverers of their city\u2019s secrets to the Keepers of their city and its destiny. To use this attainment, the mage must fix a question in her mind and being walking the streets. She will find an answer, if such an answer exists at all. This spell duplicates the effects of the Time 4 spell \u201cProphecy\u201d with Potency equal to the mage\u2019s Time dots and +1 Reach assigned to Sensory Range. The mage obtains advice on the consequences of a planned course of action or a course of action to bring about any desired result. At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, the mage may walk for one hour or one day, but she must keep walking until she gets her answer. Ariadne\u2019s thread will eventually lead the mage to a series of symbols that give her answer. Although the answer may not be apparent to any companion to the mage, she will understand its meaning and what the geomantic meditation is telling her. If the city does not know the answer to the question, or the question is too vague, the thread may lead the mage in circles or nowhere at all.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Optional Arcanum: Fate 4</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the mage also has Fate 4, she finds that her city bolsters her resolve to accomplish her task. She gains the benefit of the Fate 3 spell \u201cSuperlative Luck,\u201d with a Potency equal to her Fate dots, for any roll related to acting on the information learned during the Geomantic Meditation. +1 Reach is assigned to Instant activation; +2 Reach is assigned so that this effect works with ritual spell-casting rolls dedicated to acting on the information learned by using this attainment.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>EDIT:</b> Assigned Reach to Sensory Range. This is the reconstruction of the First Edition attainment. I added the optional Fate component because it's in keeping with the House of Ariadne's theme and beliefs.<br /> <br /> Does this stuff work or is it totally off the wall?</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","user":"Troy","date":".  Edited Reach assignments. 05-23-2016, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:25:12-07:00","id":896543,"title":"","content":"In the fifth attainment, what is the benefit of having the Reach used on Advanced Duration? At most this would mean the House of Ariadne gains the benefits of Prophecy once per Gnosis Ritual Interval (Which admittedly could be pretty awesome at high Gnosis). I'd move the Reach to Sensory Range so that it can interact with Temporal Sympathy though. You should probably take that into consideration with the rest of your attainments as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-23-2016, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:47:42-07:00","id":896759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=896543#post896543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the fifth attainment, what is the benefit of having the Reach used on Advanced Duration? At most this would mean the House of Ariadne gains the benefits of Prophecy once per Gnosis Ritual Interval (Which admittedly could be pretty awesome at high Gnosis). I'd move the Reach to Sensory Range so that it can interact with Temporal Sympathy though. You should probably take that into consideration with the rest of your attainments as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. Here's more a philosophical question, though... Is it really sensory range? My Metropolitan is in physical contact with her city when she's using her Attainments even if it's not obvious. And when I played a Metropolitan, it was obvious that she was using her abilities. She would kneel down and touch the street, listen to the walls, sit in the chair or car she was examining in order to experience the city's history.<br /> <br /> The Advanced Duration thing was because I keep thinking, &quot;This is only going to last one turn...&quot; And most of these attainments could be used for entire scenes, you know? You're going to sit on the park bench and just watch the previous day unfold. Or you're looking for a lost child in your neighborhood and you'll spend all night following Ariadne's thread to him. Do you think that's unnecessary?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Also, when you're using something on yourself, to perceive things, like &quot;Interconnections&quot; or something... is the subject of the spell yourself ... or the things you intend to examine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","user":"Troy","date":". 05-23-2016, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:58:47-07:00","id":896766,"title":"","content":"It's sensory range because the actual time that you're targeting cannot be sensed or reached by your mundane abilities. It makes total sense for them to commune with the city physically for their answers, but in the mechanics of the game a Reach still gets spent for Sensory. If it makes you feel better you can think of it as reach out to touch not only the stone of today, but of yesterday/tomorrow as well, communing with the city on its entire temporal spectrum which you simply can't do with mundane senses. <br /> <br /> You don't need Advanced Duration to cast a spell, all the effects occur at the end. If feeding the pigeons is a necessary ritual to achieve the effects of the spell the results of the spell still only need to be Instant. Walking the Thread doesn't need to be the spell itself (Though have a look at Correspondence from Space which basically does what Thread Walking did minus hints of significant threads from Fate) as it could also easily be the ritual scene that kicks the spell off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:24:30-07:00","id":896789,"title":"","content":"Thank you.<br /> <br /> Yes, walking the Thread is the pretty much the scene-long activation for most of the Attainments of the House of Ariadne.<br /> <br /> I forget that Temporal Sympathy applies to the <i>Time you are viewing</i> rather than your connection to thing you're viewing. It wasn't as explicit in First Edition and I treated it differently. Of course I can't &quot;touch the street yesterday&quot; without my Time 2 attainment for Temporal Sympathy. Thanks for helping me grok that concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T10:36:29-07:00","id":896930,"title":"","content":"So I thought about converting the Blank Badges. The core mentions them as Acanthis using symbolims of anomity with and I'm going with it. I couldn't find a way to make Fate or Time work for them so I went with Prime as secondary. So here iis what i created. Changed a few things but tried to keep the &quot;Invisibles&quot; feel to them.<br /> <br /> Name: Blank Badges<br /> Legacy Arcanum: Mind<br /> Optional Arcanum: Prime<br /> Example Yantras: Acting against the rules in a way that poses risk to the mage (+2), breaking taboos (+1),<br /> Example Oblations: Participating in &quot;alternative&quot; culture, Attending a meeting not invited, Blending in the crowd. Escaping pushinment from authority.<br /> Requirements: the recruit needs at least two dots in Occultation. Accesing the higher lvl attainments requires aditional dots. Higher lvl attainments require also dots in Subtefuge<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Attainment: Us or them<br /> Req: Mind 1, Occultation 2<br /> When you're fighting in a secret war you need to know who you can trust (to a certain degree) and who you can't. This effect mimics the effects of the spell Mental Scan though the only information the mage can gleam is how the subject feels towards the Badges ideology. The possible results are aproves/indifferent/disaproves.<br /> Optional: Prime 1<br /> In addition the mage can pierce any lies told by &quot;the enemy&quot; (everyone that got registered as &quot;disaproves&quot; by the basic version of the attainments). </div> </div> </div>I had some problems with coming up the first attainments but I think they're ok<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Attainment: We are Legion<br /> Req: Mind 2, Occultation 3<br /> The mage can become a part of a collective perfectly blending in the crowd becoming anonymous. This replicates the effect of the spell Incognito presence but it can only be used if there's a big enough group of people to blend in. This effects gets an aditional reach to access advanted duration but the mage must be part of a group of sleepers for it to work.<br /> Optional: Prime 2<br /> The mage's Nimbus becomes nondescript as if an amalganam of many. This mimics the spell Cloak Nimbus with the exception that he distays a collective Nimbus of the Legacy. This makes investigation incredibly hard but is a fairly specifc effect and someone who has previously seen a Nimbus of a member of the legacy using this attainment can recognise the effect. </div> </div> </div>These felt pretty much natural<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3 Attainment: Not a Number<br /> Req: Mind 3, Occultation 4<br /> The mage not only blends into the crowd, he trully belongs and knows how to act. When interacting with a group the mage gains dots equal to his mind dots in a single skill that would allowhim to blend better with the group. While speaking with members of a street gang he gets dots in streetwise or larcery. Running in a marathon would grant athletics, while attenting a activist gathering grant dots in politics. The mage must have at least one dot in the skill.<br /> Optional: Prime 3<br /> The mage can hide himself or his spells as the effect of Supernal Veill with an additional 1 Reach to spend (mostly used to access advanced duration) </div> </div> </div>Nothing awesome here but i think the effects fit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4 Attainment: Sleeper agent<br /> Req: Mind 4, Occultation 5, Subtefuge 2<br /> We're fighting a invisible war here and even though you never heard about it, you already picked a side.The mage can recruit a Sleeper to help him with his endeavors. The target becomes a retainer to the mage with dots equal to his Mind dots. This effect lasts for a scene and the sleeper forgets everything that happened during that time.<br /> Optional: Prime 4<br /> The Sleeper also becomes a Sleepwalker for the duration as the spell Stealing the Fire </div> </div> </div>Now this one I'm quite proud about. In the &quot;Invisibles&quot; is a recurring motive that the agents were so deeply undercover that even they didn't know they were part of the Invisibles. I think it really fits and is quite cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5 Attainment: Nothing is forbidden<br /> Req: Mind 5, Occultation 5, Subtefuge 4<br /> At this level the mage can control the way the collective reacts towards him. He doesn't manipulate inviduals, he manipulates groups or societies. He can utilize the spell Social Networking.<br /> Optional: Prime 5<br /> When the mage uses the 4th attainment it also can also leave a lasting impression on the target. The Sleeper gains an obsession related to furthering the cause of the Blanks, the exact nature of the obsession is dependant on the storyteller. This effect is Lasting. </div> </div> </div>So how do you see this ? Any suggestions. I know I forgot about the Gnosis requirements but assume they're there :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 05-23-2016, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T15:00:08-07:00","id":897233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=896338#post896338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>First Attainment: Urban Communion</b></span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once attuned to the city, she is its mother, sister, daughter, all at once. The Metropolitan spends one scene in communion with her city by whatever means she deems appropriate: a morning jog; feeding the pigeons in the park; reading the morning news in a random coffee shop; tagging graffiti in an alley; people-watching from a bus stop bench. For one day, the mage finds it exceedingly easy to get anywhere she wants to go in her city. This attainment works similarly to the spell \u201cGreen Light / Red Light\u201d: doors open for the Metropolitan, taxis and elevators arrive in the knick of time, and she never catches a red light or construction detour, etc. Reach is used for Advanced Duration.</span></i></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this Attainment can be always active. It is limited compared to the original spell, since it can't be cast offensively. It's very similar to the 11th Question Attainment, which is also always on. Since this power is about getting places quickly, the City should help right away and not require jumping through hoops, unlike in other Attainments. Also, making in permanent underscores the relationship between the Legacy and the City.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T20:38:14-07:00","id":900637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=897233#post897233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this Attainment can be always active. It is limited compared to the original spell, since it can't be cast offensively. It's very similar to the 11th Question Attainment, which is also always on. Since this power is about getting places quickly, the City should help right away and not require jumping through hoops, unlike in other Attainments. Also, making in permanent underscores the relationship between the Legacy and the City.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had considered making that First Attainment a permanently active ability, but there weren't guidelines for that in the Legacy Attainment write-up. I also didn't quite get the impression that the Eleventh Question ability was permanently active, but I can definitely see that as it's written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:35:03-07:00","id":901204,"title":"","content":"That's fair. Hopefully, more information will be available through the FAQ. Even if not, Dave's Legacies update should provide a few more points of reference. I'm very fond of always-on effects, since they show how transformative joining a Legacy can be, but I might overdo it at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T23:59:03-07:00","id":901821,"title":"","content":"Celestial Orrery Rough Draft (Further fixes) One thing I'm not entirely sure on, does looking into the future require Temporal Sympathy? On the one hand it makes sense, you're reaching into a Time that isn't the Present, on the other hand there's this quote from the book and the fact that the 11Q spends Reach to hit Sensory Range which implies (But doesn't directly state) the use of Temporal Sympathy. It could just as easily be about the advantage of being able to look at a target to determine what it will do next and how to get it to do what you want to do without having to touch it. This is kind of important in terms of the Augurs which as I've noted don't give much of a damn about changing the past since they focus on the future. That being said, I'm going to change up the 3rd and 4th attainments specifically to more closely mimic the original legacy. Does it cost a Reach to combine spells? It's late so I could really use the clarification. Thanks guys: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magic that affects the \u201cunspun\u201d time of the future is unaffectedby temporal sympathy; the shifting potential timelines have no \u201csubstance\u201d for magic to contend with </div> </div> </div>Keep the Oblations, needs Yantras<br /> <br /> Attainments:<br /> <br /> 1)<br /> Time: Momentary Flux Reach spent for Instant activation<br /> Prime: Pierce Deception Reach spent on Instant activation<br /> <br /> 2)<br /> Time: Divination Reach spent on Instant activation and Sensory Range.<br /> Prime: Made up Compelling (Or Ruling) effect to duplicate the 1e effect of a Hallow paying the mana cost of a spell equal to Potency (Though it can't exceed the amount of mana currently in the Hallow). Reach spent on Instant activation.<br /> <br /> 3)<br /> Time: Combines the effects of Shield of Chronos and Constant Presence. Reach is spent for Instant Activation and Advance Duration.<br /> Prime: Sacred Geometry Reach for Advanced and Indefinite Duration as well as the +1 Reach Clause<br /> <br /> 4)<br /> Time: Temporal version of Web Weaver. Reach is spent on Instant Activation and Sensory Range<br /> Prime: Words of Truth. Reach spent for Instant Activation, Advanced Scale and the Reach Clause of the spell.<br /> <br /> 5)<br /> Time: Prophecy: One Reach spent for Instant Activation and the Sensory Range.<br /> Prime: This mimics the effects of Geomancy with Reach spent on Advanced and Indefinite Duration and all left over Reach being spent on an effect to convert a Node into a Hallow with dots equal to Potency (2 if I understand secondary factors correctly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-29-2016, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T14:21:12-07:00","id":903003,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>, I don't think you need Temporal Sympathy to view a subject's future. You may need Sensory Range to do it without touching a subject, though. It would explain palm readers and The Dead Zone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T17:53:11-07:00","id":903140,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think you're right. Updates done, and I think that's all set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-29-2016, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:56:30-07:00","id":906027,"title":"","content":"Well here is my contribution to the community, it is just an idea; I'm <i><b>OPEN</b></i> (pun intended) to suggestions:<br /> <br /> <b>Pneumatofagoi</b> (&quot;\u03a0\u03bd\u03b5\u03c5\u03bc\u03b1\u03c4\u03bf\u03c6\u03ac\u03b3\u03bf\u03b9&quot;, pronounced &quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">pnevmatof\u00e1gi&quot;</span></span></span>, Greek for &quot;Spirit-Eaters&quot;)<br /> Ruling Arcana: Spirit<br /> Optional: Death<br /> Path: Moros<br /> Order: Free Counsil (former Nameless)<br /> Yantra: acts dedicated to satisfaction or intimidation of spirits (+1), ephemera (+1), target spirit's bane (+2)<br /> Oblations: Perform a favor for a spirit, eat a spirit, allow spirit to possess you willingly, spent some time into the Shadow<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Somehow feast from a spirit. Either consume ephemera, a materialized part or find a way to process essense.<br /> <br /> <b>Legacy History &amp; Principle:</b><br /> Members of the Legacy proudly claim that it was created near the end of the Golden Age of Athens (circa 410 BC) by awakened Sophists (Teachers and Sages) that rejected Platotic (even maybe Atlantean) cosmology and retoric. Both Sleeper and Awakened lore suggests that Sophists were heavily critisised by prominent figures, like Plato and Aristophanis, as glorified hairsplitting wordsmiths with malevolent intentions.<br /> <br /> While plato-inspired mages leaned towards following a path through the inner self -suggesting astral travels, goetia and finally accention-, the pneumatofagoi believed that they should remain fettered in the fallen world, understanding and becoming one with the world around them. They considered &quot;The Silver Ladder of Accention&quot; either a fool's Utopia or a very difficult task at hand. Supernal magic had its limits and was easily corrupted by the mortal world. No, they needed something else...<br /> <br /> Past Alexander's Time, while the proto-Diamond maped the basis of Astral realms, Pneumatofagoi were experimenting across the Gauntlet. They were facinated by the harmony of the spirit ecosystem and by their paradox-free powers. Driven by their lust to free themselves from the limits of their mortal magick, they shaped their very souls into spirits through the most efficient (and natural to their eyes) way; by becoming part of the ecosystem, devouring spirits.<br /> <br /> Pneumatofagoi that trap two or three spirits into themselves are decent company. But there are always people that want to test their limits. Present Members of the legacy are still treated with suspicion since part of the Legacy is hidding its own nature. Some extremists go as far to say that the legacy openly suggests accepting the lie (namely the shadow) and leave the supernal to the Exarchs, making it a thorn into the newly prestigious image of the Free Counsil as Enemies of the lie. Some Consilii have declared it Left-Handed or Weapon of the Enemy but no Convocation has condemned it thus far. <br /> <br /> As a old Hierarch of Athens put it &quot;You want Spirits to start talking? If you don't have a werewolf clan around, a Pneumatofagos is your next buddy on the list&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments:</b><br /> <i><b>Sapor Corporis</b></i> (1st, Know Spirit, instant +1R, sympathetic +1R +1Mana, no optional):<br /> As an instant action and by spending one Mana, you can eat a part of spiritual residue (be it leaked essense, ephemera, materialised part, etc) and one piece of knowledge per Spirit dots you possess about the specific spirit as per Know Spirit. Name, Rank, list of Manifestations, List of Numina, list of Influences and their strength, Ban, Bane.<br /> <i><b>Pneumatopagida</b></i> (2nd, Opener of the Way, Advance Duration +1R, optional Death Soul Jar):<br /> Literaly meaning &quot;Spirit-trap&quot;, by spenting one scene and taking an action relevant to the Resonant Condition, you can modify it into an Open one for one scene per Spirit dots. For example this may be done by killing something for a murder Resonant Condition or kiss someone for love/lust Resonant one. Remember that the subject might be virtualy anything, a place, a person, an item, etc. <b>Optional</b> (Death 2): By adding banning concepts (circle of salt, runes, etc) into the action, the subject of the Open Condition becomes a trap. The Open Subject functions as a &quot;Soul Jar&quot; but for spirits. The spirit can't leave the subect, possess others outside boundary (if any), or directly target the subject (but influencing others, or pushing other objects is fair game).<br /> <b><i>Signa Invisibilia</i></b> (3rd, Supress Aura, passive): You can become spiritualy invisible. You can hide any spirit or spirit-related effect on yourself from an other spirit or the Spirit arcanum including your Spirit Rank and notoriety in the spirit world. Supernatural powers to detect your spirit-stuff or to identify you as Spirit-Eater trigger a Clash of Wills. By spending one mana you can also hide one target (spirit or effect not in yourself) for one scene.<br /> <i><b>Haunted Body</b></i> (4th, Craft Fetish): Usually applied on a defeated spirit, instead of allowing it to hybernate back into the shadow, you force it inside your body creating as per Craft Fetish, gaining one influence dot or Numina per Spirit dot for up to one week.You can prolong the duration by eating large pieces of spirit corpus with your first attainment for 1 day per corpus consumed. You can have multiple hybernating spirits stiched into yourself but you can only have dots and numina in your &quot;active&quot; arsenal as your Spirit dots. You can shuffle between them by spending one action and one Mana or Essence as you change your spirit-stuff. While in this state the action becomes visible despite the invisiblility granted by the 3rd Attainment. Also, remember that Spirits can wake and break free without other powers banning them.<br /> <b><i>Spirit-Whole</i></b> (5th, No Existing Spell): By spending one Mana you can substitute all your physical attributes with a fettered spirit's Attributes (Power for Strength, Finesse for Dexterity, Resistance for Stamina), size and you can use all its powers with the spirit's stats. Doing so wakes the spirit that manifests superimposed in your body, creating something that resebles a Ridden, a spirit-human hybrid. You must roll a clash of wills each turn to remain in control. Failure means the spirit can treat you as possessed for this scene. Optional (Death): Alternatively, You can devour one of the spirits you fettered into yourself -killing it instantly- gaining powers from that spirit as with previous attainment but fettered with Indefinite Duration. These powers are excluded from the previous attainment restrictions. You can have up 5 Indefinite fettered Powers in your arsenal (in addition to the previous attainment). By activating the Devour-Attainment again you can permanently remove (painfuly riping spirit parts apart from you, or the spirit parts forcibly get out) granted powers for new ones respecting the attainments limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","user":"Shadowjim12","date":". 06-02-2016, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T23:48:04-07:00","id":906257,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6169_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6169\" data-vbnamecard=\"6169\">Shadowjim12</a> , interesting, I will show my partner that has Spirit Moros in our London game and looks for Legacy for him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T04:08:31-07:00","id":938724,"title":"","content":"This is the adaptation of the Forge Masters my Storyteller and I cooked up and we would like your opinion on it. I copied most of the structure from Shadowjim12\u2019s post since it was really well worked out, thanks for that.<br /> <br /> <b>Forge masters </b>(Powersmiths)<br /> Ruling Arcana: Prime<br /> Optional: Matter<br /> Path: Moros<br /> Order: Free Council<br /> <br /> Initiation, History, Yantra\u2019s and Oblations are all similar to the original Legacy since that was pretty much as good as it was going to get. But for those of you unfamiliar with the Legacy: Powersmiths are item crafters and are especially known for working with Thaumium. They strongly favour working with metal, which is also the material they use for their Grimoires.<br /> <br /> With regard to the Duration of all the Attainments we planned to follow the scheme laid out in the original Legacy. There a Forge master had to spend a turn working on an object he wanted to apply an Attainment on to make it last for an entire scene. If he spent an entire scene working on an object then the Attainment will last a day. Otherwise we would have it last as many rounds as the lowest Arcanum of Matter and Prime.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments:</b><br /> <b><i>Metal Grimoire</i></b> (1st, Scribe Grimoire):<br /> The Forge masters are known for working wonders with metals and this first Attainment is evidence of that. It is far easier to hide a Grimoire as a ring or bracelet than a book. The size of the Grimoire determines the number of Rotes that can be stored on a linear basis (Size 1 = 1 Rote, Size 2 = 2 Rotes). <u>Optional</u>: Matter, The Powersmith\u00b4s Matter dots determine the maximum dot rating of the Rotes stored.<br /> <b><i>Upgrade </i></b>(2nd, Find the balance and As above so below):<br /> With even the slightest adjustment tools can be made so much better, the affected object gains the 9-again quality both for its intended purpose as a tool and for its symbolic purpose as a Yantra. <u>Optional</u>: By spending 1 Mana during the activation of the Attainment one of its purposes becomes further improved and instead gains the 8-again quality. By spending 2 Mana both of its purposes are so reinforced.<br /> <b><i>True tools</i></b> (3rd, Ephemeral enchantment, Shrink and grow):<br /> Works like Ephemeral enchantment. Optional: Adjust the size category of the enchanted object up or down up to the Mage\u2019s dots in Matter. (Alternative suggestions are very welcome).<br /> <b><i>In the forge of its making</i></b> (4th, Nigredo and albedo/Annihilate matter):<br /> Many are the legends about items that can only be destroyed on the very anvil that was used to create them (does a specific Ring come to mind?). This Attainment does exactly that: You can destroy objects utterly. This also applies to Artifacts, but with consequences. When using the Attainment on an Artifact it creates a backlash and the Forge Master will take Lethal damage equal to the Merit rating or Equipment bonus of the Artifact. Optional: By spending Mana during the destruction of an Artifact the Mage can reduce the damage of the backlash on a 1 for 1 basis.<br /> <b><i>From memory</i></b> (5th, Ex Nihilo):<br /> At the pinnacle of reforging his soul the Forge Master\u2019s soul has become a forge itself and can use it as such. The Forge Master can at any moment reproduce any item he has worked on. Optional: Upon creating an object, immediately apply one of the other Attainments to it.<br /> <br /> We know that the next book (Signs of Power I believe?) will finally give us a lot more information on Perfected metals and we will likely incorporate those in the Legacy. For now we are going to go with this, but we would really appreciate any constructive feedback you could give us. Suggestions for different Attainments are very welcome since we mostly stuck to known spells instead of trying to think up unusual Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T05:42:31-07:00","id":938753,"title":"","content":"2nd attainment's mana cost, attainments shouldn't charge more than one mana. You may want to add restrictions or bump it up on the attainment level if you want to achieve balance you seem to be looking for.<br /> <br /> 4th attainment seems to actually be mimicking an Unmaking effect, on top of that it shouldn't work on artifacts. Mana cost that doesn't follow the rules again.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of using As Above so Below and the metal grimoire, you may want to do something that tinkers with how Imbuing works to get that magic weapon smith feel. For instance, what if for the 4th attainment a Smith can Imbue an object with the spells he's inscribed into the object as a grimoire getting some kind of benefit like reduced spell control cost, or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-28-2016, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T08:49:41-07:00","id":938878,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Thank you for your reply.<br /> <br /> 2nd Attainment: I have to disagree with you on the subject of how much mana Attainments should charge. The description of the Mana break paragraph of the Legacy section only mentions that any existing mana costs should be reduced to either 0 or 1. However, the 9-again to 8-again upgrade in both Find the balance and As above so below is a Reach effect, which is why we decided to put the price of 1 mana on that upgrade. It never had a mana cost associated with it, so it should not fall under the purview of the Mana break paragraph.<br /> Now I would like your opinion on what you think would be the best solution to this: 1. Remove the option completely, limiting the Attainment to the 9-again quality, 2. Keep the current solution, 3. Keep the mana cost, but limit the possible 8-again quality to either function, 4. Something else.<br /> <br /> As for limitations, it could very well be that Upgrade could only be used on metal objects.<br /> <br /> 4th Attainment: The effect of destroying Artifacts is indeed an Unmaking effect, but destroying things also falls under Fraying (Nigredo and Albedo for Matter, there are more in other Arcana). Using Annihilate Matter can destroy Artifacts and is about the only way I have been able to find to so, but it does indeed cost a Reach and a point of mana to use that option. That was the reason we built in the Supernal backlash, as a sign that the Mage is overreaching. That backlash can be mitigated by spending a ton of mana, which is again not part of the original spell.<br /> <br /> I will admit that, to us as well, the effect feels wonky and a bit out of place. But we really wanted an Attainment that was a counterbalance to all the enhancing and creating options already in there, to prevent the Legacy from becoming too much of a one-trick pony. I also wanted to include the aspect of mystical smithing that deals with how to get rid of dangerous items: Taking it back to the forge in which is was made.<br /> <br /> Your suggestion for Imbueing items sounds very interesting, but could you elaborate a bit more? What I think you are trying to say is this: a Powersmith could be able to Imbue items with spells that he has in a metal Grimoire (which he uses during the process) without it costing him spell control slots. I agree that would be an awesome alternative 4th Attainment and would mesh well with the image of a magical smith, but I am pretty sure that would be way off on the balance side of things. Which is why I am not sure if I am understanding you correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:22:11-07:00","id":939076,"title":"","content":"Rereading, 1st attainment I think you could get away with dots in Matter increase the number of rotes that can be stored on an item Matter+Size.<br /> <br /> I don't know how you spent the Reach that attainments are supposed to have so I'm not really able to give an informed opinion on what you should do with the 2nd attainment. You could get an extra Reach by making the attainment take a scene to activate which would reduce the need to overcharge players on mana.<br /> <br /> 4th Attainment, the lesser effects you reference have no effect on Artifacts at all, and if you've read the errata the Reach for Annihilate Matter in order to effect Artifacts has been removed, this is on top of the fact that you're trying to force a 5th dot effect into a 4th dot slot. I just reflexively really don't like that. It's cool if you want to use it as a way to destroy Imbued items, but since Artifacts originate from the Supernal (Or Archmasters) you're (Probably) never going to be able to access &quot;the forge on which they were created.&quot; That should be less an inherent power and more of a plot hook. Also, Forge Masters are sort of a one trick pony, but there's nothing wrong with that, most Legacies are. It's their &quot;trick&quot; that's part of what makes them interesting. That's just my opinion though. I'd either change the attainment to be about destroying things (Including Imbued items) or about Perfecting metals which can then be forged into the magical alloys like Orihalcum. Another option is to have the Prime part be basically Supernal Dispellation, (Or maybe Celestial Fire for the fires of the forge kind of feel) and the Matter Optional to be metal Perfecting. I'd play around with it, your &quot;Optional&quot; for the 4th attainment the way it is right now isn't really doing anything interesting.<br /> <br /> My first thought was indeed that a Powersmith would be able to Imbue items without using up spell control slots, but as you pointed out that's a bit ridiculous. Instead, I'd suggest making it so that spells imbued into an item become bundled. So let's say you have an object and it has the space to hold 4 Rotes with your Metal Grimoire ability. You can inscribe the Rotes and then Imbue the item with the same spells as the Rotes, and all of the spells on the item take only 1 spell control slot. This is pretty potent, but heck you're a Master at that point anyway and at least there is still -some- limit. It's not that bonkers either, it's basically a way to break Combined Spells a bit by decoupling them from their need to share Factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T03:47:51-07:00","id":939428,"title":"","content":"Really? Annihilate Matter was erratad to no longer affect Artifacts? Could you provide me with the link to that errata? Since I went over the most recent list of errata and it does not even mention Annihilate Matter, so I would like to know what else I missed. It makes sense though, since none of the other Arcana can touch Artifacts as well.<br /> <br /> With the 1st Attainment I would instead go for something in between the current 2 options, such as using Size + Matter to determine the amount of Rotes based on the rank of the Rotes. So a Matter 3 Mage can store 4 dots worth of Rotes in a Size 1 object. This is mostly related to physical restrictions. otherwise a Master of Matter could store 6 Rotes in a Size 1 ring, but that would make it really hard to find the carvings/etchings that make it function as a Grimoire. I would also think that higher level spells require more elaboration = more space.<br /> <br /> The 2nd Attainment would then end up something like this: 9-again quality normally, if you spend a whole scene giving it an Upgrade it will give the 8-again quality, but you do not get the day long Duration that you would normally get for working on something for a scene.<br /> <br /> 4th Attainment, funny that you should mention the Celestial Fire as a representation of the fires of a forge, that was exactly why I included it in my original set of potential 4th level Attainments. In the end we decided not to use it since it did not really mesh well with the rest. I think we will keep it limited to destroying Imbued items, but not Artifacts, and tass since that is a part of both Prime and Matter. We already planned to switch it out for something to do with Perfected Metals, but sadly Prime currently does not allow for that. Which is something that felt really off about the original Forge masters. They focussed on and are known for working with Perfected Metals, but with their Arcana (disregarding that they typically come from Moros and thus should have an affinity for Death) they cannot actually create Perfected Metals. It is one the Prime reasons why I am really looking forward to the next book.<br /> <br /> The bundling of spells would indeed also lead to a massive reduction in spell controll slots needed. Bundle enchantments was actually one of my favourite spells from the Tome of the Mysteries, so that might be a direction to start looking into. Food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T06:25:08-07:00","id":939487,"title":"","content":"Double checked the errata, my mistake, I was thinking of Word of Unmaking (Prime) which is kind of vague even after the errata because it lumped Supernal Artifacts in with &quot;magic items&quot; as not being destructible usually, but the Reach clause allows for the destruction of magic items, but the errata says to remove the mention of artifacts. Still, knowing the origin of Artifacts I feel pretty confident saying they probably shouldn't be something a Mage can destroy under normal circumstances.<br /> <br /> 1st attainment, that's what I mean, size X + X dots in Matter determines Grimoire space. I wouldn't worry about the carvings or etchings being hard to find or whatever just because you're jamming a lot of them into one small space. Just as a tangent, in 1e Powersmiths had the ability to instantly analyze magical items to determine function and activation and they don't have that here.<br /> <br /> 2nd attainment, that seems like a reasonable solution.<br /> <br /> 4th attainment if you make Prime able to degrade magical items and tass (Which might outright destroy them, but it's no Word of Unmaking) and then use your Matter Optional to deal with Perfected Metals you get the best of both worlds.<br /> <br /> 5th attainment: Mind you bundling spell control only takes up your Prime attainment, so you still have something to figure out with Matter for the Optional (Can't remember if you had that already).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T05:06:00-07:00","id":940051,"title":"","content":"I feel kind of bad about this, but I found another conversion of the Forge Masters that could serve as a better basis than what I cooked up with my friend. It will require some small adjustments, but should better fit within the current Reach constraints. Here is the quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ansgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885225-2e-errata-needed-problem-with-legacies-attainments-as-written?p=885762#post885762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the initiation requirements for a legacy's first attainment require the ruling arcanum at 2-dots. Does that mean that both the first and second attainments can be built with one-dot spells with +2 reach? By spending two reach for Advanced Duration and Indefinite Duration you can make any attainment effect permanent? So it would be possible for a Spirit or Death legacy to have a see spirits/ghosts spell as a permanent effect for the first attainment.<br /> <br /> Legacy creation was my favorite part of 1st Ed and I was pretty salty when I saw how much weaker 2nd Ed legacies seemed to be. But it's not that bad. 1st Ed legacies can be converted to 2nd Ed by increasing the attainments two levels. so 1st, 2nd, and 3rd attainments become 3rd, 4th, and 5th attainments. Assuming the spells used didn't change practices in the edition change, the functionality should be mostly the same. The converted attainments only have their Gnosis and Arcana requirements increased by one point, which isn't bad.<br /> <br /> 1st Ed legacies typically either had active powers with scene long duration or passive powers with indefinite duration, and almost never had attainments based on attack or healing spells. This can be kept in 2nd Ed by taking the Instant Action and Advanced Duration reaches for active powers and Advanced Duration and Indefinite Duration for passive powers. Some legacies will have problems with spells being limited to touch range, requiring another reach for sensory range.<br /> <br /> I worked on the Forge Masters last night. Here's what I came up with. I assumed that the Analyze Enchanted Item ability of the first attainment is now a function of Focused Prime Sight and didn't address it in the 2nd Ed attainments. Primal Tempering did lose the ability to inflict aggravated damage to Twilight beings as that would have required an additional +2 Reach.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Third:</b> The Master\u2019s Hand<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 4, Prime 3, Craft 3<br /> <b>Reach:</b> Instant Action, Advanced Duration<br /> <br /> As an instant action the mage can attune himself to an item suitable for use as a tool Yantra and gain 9-again on all spellcasting rolls when using the tool. Only the most recently attuned object gains this benefit.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Matter 3<br /> <b>Reach:</b> Instant Action, Advanced Duration, 8-Again<br /> <br /> The mage examines an item as an instant action, learning its purpose and how to properly use it. If something is keeping the item from functioning as intended, the mage knows what the problem is. The mage gains 8-again on all rolls when using the item for its intended purpose. Only the most recently studied object gains this benefit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fourth:</b> Primal Tempering<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 6, Prime 4, Craft 4<br /> <b>Reach:</b> Instant Action, Advanced Duration<br /> <br /> As an instant action the mage can imbue an item with power and make it solid to all Twilight entities. The attainment only applies to the item\u2019s primary purpose. A ghost could type on a typewriter enhanced with Primal Tempering but could not pick it up and use it as a bludgeoning weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Matter 4<br /> <b>Reach:</b> Instant Action, Advanced Duration (additional spell factors assigned to duration)<br /> <br /> Items enhanced with Primal Tempering also have their Durability increased by a number of points equal to the mage\u2019s dots in Matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fifth:</b> Primal Forge<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 8, Prime 5, Craft 5<br /> <b>Reach:</b> Instant Action, Advanced Duration (additional spell factors assigned to duration)<br /> <br /> The mage no longer requires a forge to work his magic. As an instant action he may spend a point of Mana and manifest a Supernal symbol in physical form. His conjurations can be as complex as simple mechanical items, including weapons and armor. He gains a number of points to spend equal to his dots in Prime to allocate to the item\u2019s Durability, equipment bonus, and Mana pool. The item starts with a Durability and Mana pool of 1.<br /> <br /> The item\u2019s Mana pool comes prefilled with Mana and one point is consumed each turn the item is used as part of a non-spellcasting dice roll. Once all of the Mana points have been spent the item dissolves. The mage can use Channel Mana to refill the Mana pool. When the item\u2019s duration elapses it dissolves and all remaining Mana is lost.<br /> <br /> Conjured items may be further enhanced with Primal Tempering or imbued with spells.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Matter 5<br /> <b>Reach:</b> Instant Action, Advanced Duration (additional spell factors assigned to duration)<br /> <br /> The item gains the Durability increase from Primal Tempering and the item can be constructed from a perfected metal.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Ansgar suggests, I would make the 1st Attainment vision based, since I actually forgot about the fact that Powersmiths could instantly identify Imbued items. However, instead of Mage sight I would change that to Supernal vision, with Craftsman's eye as the Optional Matter inclusion. That way you could know both if an item was Imbued an what its intended purpose is.<br /> <br /> Ansgar does not mention a 2nd Attainment, but for that we could easily use the Metal Grimoire as we worked it out above. In this version we could even use the now available Reach to give the option to spend 1 Mana (you already get the Mana Break since creating a Grimoire usually costs 1 Mana) to make the Grimoire of Lasting Duration, while still keeping the Matter + Size = number of Rote dots worth of space in the Grimoire.<br /> <br /> The 3rd Attainment works perfectly as described, but I would make the distribution of the 8 and 9-again qualities optional. I know this goes against the Legacy rulings of fixed Reach, but the Reach is still relatively fixed I would argue. Let me know what you think. I would also be fine with the 8-again quality on the intended purpose, but I think my option is more fun.<br /> <br /> Primal Tempering is fine, but the Advanced duration Reach is a bit wasted because of the way the Forge Masters handle that (I will repeat this at the end). Instead I would use the Reach now available to use the Advanced Scale factor since the one thing better than one Primally tempered typewriter is multiple Primally tempered typewriters. I also still think that increasing Durability as an optional is a bit of a tame ability, but considering that it could also be used to create an army of Primally Tempered Golems sort of makes up for that. <br /> <br /> I do still think that Primal Forge should be based on Ex nihilo instead of Platonic form and as such I would keep using the version we have hammered out (pun intended) during the earlier posts which included automatically Imbueing it or giving the option of bundling enchantments.<br /> <br /> As for the Advanced Duration Reach being less useful for Forge Masters I will repeat what I mentioned in my first post: With regard to the Duration of all the Attainments we planned to follow the scheme laid out in the original Legacy. There a Forge master had to spend a turn working on an object he wanted to apply an Attainment on to make it last for an entire scene. If he spent an entire scene working on an object then the Attainment will last a day. Otherwise we would have it last as many rounds as the lowest Arcanum of Matter and Prime.<br /> <br /> The one detractor from this latest version is that it in no way involves creating or using Perfected Metals. So the release of the next book might make me change my opinion on this version. <br /> <br /> I will likely post a more worked out version later today or tomorrow. One with a bit more structure, instead of the current comment style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T05:44:11-07:00","id":940586,"title":"","content":"Here is the redesigned version of the Forge masters I promised to write up yesterday.<br /> <br /> <b>Forge masters </b>(Powersmiths)<br /> Ruling Arcana: Prime<br /> Optional: Matter<br /> Path: Moros<br /> Order: Free Council<br /> <br /> Initiation, History, Yantra\u2019s and Oblations are all similar to the original Legacy since that was pretty much as good as it was going to get. But for those of you unfamiliar with the Legacy: Powersmiths are item crafters and are especially known for working with Thaumium. They strongly favour working with metal, which is also the material they use for their Grimoires.<br /> <br /> With regard to the Duration of all the Attainments we planned to follow the scheme laid out in the original Legacy. There a Forge master had to spend a turn working on an object he wanted to apply an Attainment on to make it last for an entire scene. If he spent an entire scene working on an object then the Attainment will last a day. Otherwise we would have it last as many rounds as the lowest Arcanum of Matter and Prime.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Attainments:</i></b><br /> <i><b>The Master\u2019s gaze</b></i> (1st, Supernal vision, Craftsman\u2019s eye):<br /> <i>Prerequisites</i>: Prime 2, Crafts 2 and Science or Occult or Athletics at at least 2 dots.<br /> <i>Reach: </i>Instant casting.<br /> A Forge master can at will mimic the effects of the Supernal vision spell, allowing him to identify Imbued or Enhanced items and Artifacts with ease as well as their Supernal purpose. The Master\u2019s gaze activates automatically when touching one of these types of items. <u>Optional </u>(Matter 1): The Powersmith also knows the intended non-Supernal function of any object he holds when the Master\u2019s gaze is active.<br /> <b><i>Metal Grimoire</i></b> (2nd, Scribe Grimoire)<br /> <i>Prerequisites</i>: Prime 2, Crafts 3.<br /> <i>Reach: </i>Instant casting, Lasting option.<br /> The Forge masters are known for working wonders with metals and this second Attainment is evidence of that. It is far easier to hide a Grimoire as a ring or bracelet than a book. The size of the Grimoire together with the Forge Master\u2019s mastery of Matter determines the dots worth of Rotes that can be stored: Size + Matter dots = Nr. dots worth of Rotes in the Metal Grimoire. <u>Optional </u>(Matter 2): By spending 1 Mana during the activation of the Attainment the Metal Grimoire can be made Lasting.<br /> <b><i>The Master\u2019s hand</i></b> (3rd, As above so below, Alter balance):<br /> <i>Prerequisites</i>: Prime 3, Crafts 3, Science or Occult or Athletics increased to 3 dots or two of those at 2 dots.<br /> <i>Reach: </i>Instant casting, 8-again quality option.<br /> Use of the Master\u2019s hand infuses a tool with supernal meaning, granting the 9-again quality to any spellcasting roll that incorporates it as a Yantra. <u>Optional</u> (Matter 3): The Mage can choose to include the tools original function as well, granting it the 9-again quality on rolls that involve its intended purpose as well. <u>Optional</u> 2: Either of the 9-again qualities can be upgraded to the 8-again quality instead.<br /> <b><i>Primal tempering</i></b> (4th, Ephemeral enchantment):<br /> <i>Prerequisites</i>: Prime 4, Crafts 4, Science or Occult or Athletics increased to 3 dots or two of those at 2 dots.<br /> <i>Reach: </i>Instant casting, Advanced Scale (use Matter to determine Scale).<br /> As an instant action the mage can imbue an item with power and make it solid to all Twilight entities. The attainment only applies to the item\u2019s primary purpose. A ghost could type on a typewriter enhanced with Primal tempering but could not pick it up and use it as a bludgeoning weapon.<br /> Optional (Matter 4): Items enhanced with Primal Tempering also have their Durability increased by a number of points equal to the mage\u2019s dots in Matter.<br /> <b><i>Primal Forge</i></b> (5th, Ex Nihilo):<br /> <i>Prerequisites</i>: Prime 5, Crafts 4, Science or Occult or Athletics increased to 4 dots or must attain three dots in a second Skill from the list of possible requirements, or two dots in a third Skill from the list.<br /> <i>Reach: </i>Instant casting.<br /> At the pinnacle of reforging his soul the Forge Master\u2019s soul has become a forge itself and can use it as such. The Forge Master can at any moment reproduce any item he has worked on. <u>Optional</u> (Matter 5): Any spells that the Powersmith uses that target the created item count as one spell against his spell control slots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":12164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","user":"Zaephyrus","date":"see post #148-150). 07-31-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T06:13:51-07:00","id":940598,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason you're blending Matter and Prime so heavily? Like, for ephemeral enchantment why is Matter what determines the scale? It should be Prime because that's the arcana for that part of the attainment. And you switched the order of primary and optional attainment in the 5th attainment instead of keeping the normal legacy format.<br /> <br /> Other than those minor fixes I'd say this is really solid now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T08:10:04-07:00","id":940623,"title":"","content":"Yes I have a reason for blending Matter and Prime so heavily. For me the Forge masters are all about blending Matter and Prime and I would expect that someone who takes the Legacy would do so as well. Besides that I think that more Legacies should blend their two main Arcana more, since for some effects it just makes more sense for the pre-Legacy Major Arcana to be the one governing an Attainment. That is the reason why I switched the format for the last Attainment.<br /> It makes more sense to me that a legendary craftsman can instantly recreate anything they ever made and have loads of freedom to then improve on it than that he can recreate an inferior copy of something (although this can cover more complex constructs) and then have the option to reinforce said inferior copy. Then again, this is my personal opinion.<br /> <br /> As for Matter governing the Scale on Primal Tempering, that is my interpretation of the effect of taking Advanced Scale as a Reach effect in the new Reach system. The rules for Legacies state that the Legacies main Arcana governs primary spell factors. Normally this would be Duration for Ephemeral enchantment and Potency would then be governed by Matter. However, since Duration is calculated based on the amount of time spent implementing an Attainment I felt that Prime should determine Potency, as it represents the firmness with which the tool is present across all layers of reality and Matter would then govern the Scale. Granted it can be argued that Prime should still cover the Scale in that case since Potency would here mostly be used to withstand dispellation and Attainments are immune to dispellation. I do not think it Matters that much in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T09:04:24-07:00","id":940639,"title":"","content":"I'm not disagreeing about the order of the main and optional attainment in the fifth attainment, I'm just saying you should stick to the format, Prime first, Matter 2nd, in other words keep it as is and then just switch which arcana is doing what. I suppose this might mean that technically the Prime version is calling forth an Eidolon or similar of his work rather than the work itself which makes sense since to do that would actually require Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T16:01:49-07:00","id":1076688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/805117-legacies-2ed-update-ideas?p=895581#post895581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"center\"><b>Daoine</b></div> <br /> <b>First Attainment: Black Cat's Passing</b><br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> The Good Folk know the best way to punish the sins of the guilty. This attainment mimics the effects of &quot;Serendipity&quot; (p. 135), save that the Mage can only use it when she wishes to learn the most effective way to punish or hurt someone. Reach is spent on instant activation.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Time 1<br /> The Daoine spends one scene contemplating an omen she received using the first attainment. She may then ask specific questions about how her omen can come to pass, per &quot;Divination&quot; (p. 186) and its Reach effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment: The Faerie Mask</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 2, Occult 2<br /> The Daoine spends a scene in seclusion and masks her destiny, allowing her to evade the curses of others. This attainment functions as &quot;Fabricate Fortune&quot; (p. 136). Reach is spent on advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Time 2<br /> By reading the weave of Time, the Daoine may distinguish saints from sinners. This attainment functions as &quot;Momentary Flux&quot; (p. 187). Reach is spent on instant activation and sensory range.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment: The Evil Eye</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 3, Occult 3<br /> The Mage touches her victim and places a terrifying curse upon her. This attainment functions per &quot;Exceptional Luck&quot; (p. 135), save that it can only be used to place hexes on someone. Reach is spent on instant activation and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Time 3<br /> The Daoine may supplement any use of the third attainment with the effect of &quot;Hung Spell&quot; (p. 188). The effect of the hex only takes place when Hung Spell's duration expires, when the Mages chooses to relinquish the Hung Spell effect, or when some conditions set by the Fate 2 attainment Conditional Duration are met. Regardless, using this optional attainment always costs one point of mana. Reach is spent on instant activation and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment: The Eternal Wheel</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 4, Occult 4<br /> The Daoine spends one scene meditating upon the skein of destiny, after which she gains the benefits of &quot;Interconnections&quot; (p. 134). Reach is spent on Interconnections' additional Reach effects, as well as advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: Time 4</b><br /> While the main effect of the fourth attainment is active, the Daoine may spend a point of mana in order to study a specific subject under &quot;Postcognition&quot; (p. 187). This can allow the Mage to see how a subject's destiny has changed over time. Reach is spent on instant activation, sensory activation, advanced duration, and the reach effect to &quot;scrub&quot; the visions.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment: Doom of Promise</b><br /> Prerequisites: Fate 5, Occult 5<br /> The Daoine confirms an oath with a touch or handshake, sealing it with &quot;Oaths Fulfilled&quot; (p. 135). Reach is spent on instant activation, advanced duration, and all of the spell's optional Reach effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Time 5<br /> The Good Folk have no need for first chances. Whenever someone breaks an oath made with the fifth attainment's standard, the Daoine may spend one scene in meditation and spend one point of mana in order to return to the moment the oath was sanctified per &quot;Corridors of Time&quot; (p. 191). Once there, the Mage <i>must</i> curse the oathbreaker using the Legacy's third attainment, after which she returns to the present. Reach is spent on sensory activation in order to make use of Temporal Sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of my favorites Legacies. And this update works really well. I missed the concept of the Scales of Wyrd, and the concept that they sometimes bless a subject too, so I changed some little things:<br /> <br /> The name of the First Attainment is <b>First Attainment: Understanding the Scale</b>. It does not give you the best way to punish or hurt someone, but the best way to act in a way that don't provoke the Scale of Wyrd. The Optional effect is the same, but to understand why it would upset the Wyrd. Its a good initiation tool that focus on the aspect of learning how the Scale works.<br /> <br /> The Second Attainment is now the <b>Second Attainment: Black Cat's Passing</b> and works as Shifting the Odds, needing a scene to activate and spending the reach on Advanced Duration. The mage can use this to find someone who had upset the Scale of the Wyrd (translating, some transgressor). And the Optional effect is Green Light/Red Light, with Reach for Imediate use and Advanced Duration, that you can use to bless/punish a subject by touching him.<br /> <br /> The third attainment is perfect. But I really wanted to give it's name a more fitting meaning. I know that this is hardly something that every ST would permit, but in my table, the player can expend 1 mana to add sensory activation as an extra option. Also, they can bless with good fortune someone that is worth.<br /> <br /> The Fourth and Fifth attainments are amazing as they already are, so i changed nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 04-13-2017, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T00:52:59-07:00","id":1146585,"title":"","content":"Any updates on the Forge Masters Legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16351-milanwow123","name":"milanwow123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}